こんばんは！のじゃばんわー！
Good evening! Nojabanwa~!

34
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:29,500
おぬしらいかがお過ごしでしょうかー？
How is everyone doing today?

35
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:33,400
わいやばい。ね、おぬしらやばい。
I'm in trouble. Hey, you guys, I'm in trouble.

36
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,800
二日酔い大丈夫って？え、そう。
Asking if my hangover is okay? Eh, really?

37
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,300
わいやばい！ね、おぬしらやばい、助けて！
I'm in trouble! Hey, you guys, help me out!

38
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:42,300
わし、わしほろよい1缶半で二日酔いになっちゃった！
I got a hangover from drinking just 1.5 cans of Horoyoi!

39
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,100
どうしようおぬしら！
What should I do, you guys?!

40
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,900
どうすればいいかなわし？
What should I do?

41
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,800
あのさー
You know...

42
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,800
あの、お酒は残ってないと思うんじゃけど
I don't think there's alcohol left in my system, but...

43
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:57,000
あの、頭が、頭がさ、あのグワングワンする感覚
My head... my head feels like it's throbbing and spinning.

44
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,800
頭がグワングワンする感覚。
That spinning feeling in my head.

45
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,500
さっきポカリをね、一本飲んだのじゃ。
I drank a bottle of Pocari Sweat earlier, noja.

46
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:05,500
うん
Yeah.

47
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,400
ヘパリーゼも？あ、確かに！
Hepalyse too? Ah, indeed!

48
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:10,500
なんか色んなののあれかな？
Maybe it's a mix of different things?

49
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:13,500
あの、あわせ？合わせか？
A combination? A combo?

50
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,300
合わせ技か？
Is it a combo effect?

51
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,500
うん、合わせ技な気がする。
Yeah, I feel like it's a combo effect.

52
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,800
ま、でもあの、運動とかしなきゃ大丈夫じゃから
Well, but as long as I don't exercise or anything, I'll be fine, so...

53
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,800
今日は楽しくお歌を、ミネラルも摂ってね
Today we'll enjoy singing while getting some minerals too, right?

54
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
ミネラルって何で摂れるんだろう？
How do you get minerals anyway?

55
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:35,800
わしの、わしの身の回りにあるものにミネラルあるかな？
Are there things around me that have minerals?

56
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:37,800
塩とか？
Like salt?

57
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,800
ミネラルって何だ？
What is a mineral?

58
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:44,200
ミネラルって何だ？ミネラルが分からないな。
What are minerals? I don't even know what minerals are.

59
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
ミネラルウォーター？
Mineral water?

60
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,000
え
Eh?

61
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,800
漏れのこの水はミネラル入ってるのかな？
Does my water here contain minerals?

62
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,800
塩？塩とか？
Salt? Like salt?

63
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:53,900
水？
Water?

64
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,500
普通の水でいいんか？
Is regular water fine?

65
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:58,200
普通の水ってミネラル入ってるのかな？
Does regular water contain minerals?

66
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,800
難しい
That's tricky.

67
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,328
ポカリとラムネ
Pocari and Ramune...

68
00:05:02,828 --> 00:05:03,658
麦茶
Barley tea...

69
00:05:04,208 --> 00:05:06,188
わしの家に麦茶ないのじゃよ
I don't have barley tea at my house, though.

70
00:05:06,678 --> 00:05:08,568
ミネラル麦茶
Mineral barley tea.

71
00:05:09,128 --> 00:05:11,168
ちょ、麦茶を探してくるか
Wait, should I go look for barley tea?

72
00:05:11,758 --> 00:05:13,678
取りに、取りに行くか
Go... go get it?

73
00:05:13,988 --> 00:05:14,868
買いに行くか
Go buy it?

74
00:05:15,008 --> 00:05:17,658
買いに行くほど取りにいくって言ってるのやばい
Saying "go get it" as if I'm going out to buy it is crazy.

75
00:05:17,658 --> 00:05:20,588
スポーツ飲料？え、飲んだ飲んだ飲んだ！じゃあ行ける、じゃあ行けるかもわし
Sports drink? Eh, I drank it, I drank it! Then I can make it, maybe I can make it!

76
00:05:20,588 --> 00:05:22,258
ポカリ飲んだポカリ
I drank Pocari, Pocari.

77
00:05:22,258 --> 00:05:24,478
ポカリさっきね
Pocari, just earlier...

78
00:05:24,478 --> 00:05:28,168
まずいと思って「間に合え間に合え」と思って爆飲みしたのじゃ
"Oh no," I thought, and chugged it thinking "make it in time, make it in time!"

79
00:05:28,708 --> 00:05:32,448
なん…なんかきょー調子悪いなーって思って
I felt like... I felt kinda sick today, you know?

80
00:05:33,208 --> 00:05:35,328
もしかしてお酒かー？と思って
I thought, "Could it be alcohol...?"

81
00:05:36,428 --> 00:05:37,498
のじゃあ！
Yeah!

82
00:05:37,498 --> 00:05:43,088
そう、お酒かーと思って、あのポカリをね、飲みまくったのじゃ
Yeah, thinking it might be alcohol, I chugged tons of Pocari.

83
00:05:45,308 --> 00:05:50,058
「間に合え、間に合え！これ、これ二日酔い感も間に合え間に合え！」と言って
I was like, "Make it in time, make it in time! Clear up this hangover feeling in time!"

84
00:05:50,708 --> 00:05:51,988
少し楽になった
It got a little better.

85
00:05:52,328 --> 00:05:54,388
朝よりはだいぶ楽なのじゃ
I feel way better than this morning.

86
00:05:56,008 --> 00:05:57,978
睡眠が浅くなったのもあると思う
I think my sleep being shallow played a part too.

87
00:05:59,048 --> 00:06:03,388
そう、お昼からさ、ちょっとお仕事あったからさ、起きたんじゃけれど
Yeah, since I had some work in the afternoon, I woke up, but...

88
00:06:04,148 --> 00:06:06,188
だからね、あんまりたくさんいっぱいは寝れてないかも
So I might not have gotten a whole lot of sleep.

89
00:06:06,848 --> 00:06:08,568
そうなのかもしれないのじゃ
That might be why.

90
00:06:10,978 --> 00:06:13,218
「間に合え！間に合え！」
"Make it in time! Make it in time!"

91
00:06:16,278 --> 00:06:17,698
そう、ポカリ飲んだのじゃ
Yeah, I drank Pocari.

92
00:06:20,898 --> 00:06:24,428
なかなか、いや自分があそこまでお酒弱いと思わなかったなー
Man... I really didn't think I was that weak to alcohol.

93
00:06:24,898 --> 00:06:28,168
あんま配信でお酒をさ、飲むの初めてじゃったじゃろ？
It was my first time drinking alcohol on stream, right?

94
00:06:28,458 --> 00:06:30,958
初めてじゃったから気づかなかったけれど
Because it was my first time, I didn't realize, but...

95
00:06:31,068 --> 00:06:33,408
あんなに弱いと思わなかったなー
I didn't think I was that weak.

96
00:06:34,908 --> 00:06:40,708
思わなかったな、もう、もう飲酒配信は…
I really didn't think so. I can't... I can't do drinking streams anymore...

97
00:06:40,708 --> 00:06:41,528
できないね
Can't do them.

98
00:06:41,878 --> 00:06:44,208
もうメン限じゃないとこじゃできないなーってちょっと思った
I kinda felt like I can't do them anywhere outside member-only streams.

99
00:06:44,538 --> 00:06:52,328
さすがにさ、さすがに1回さ、まずやってみるか、行けるかと思ってさ、行けるかと思ってやってみたんじゃけれど
As expected, I wanted to try it once to see if I could handle it, so I tried it, but...

100
00:06:54,188 --> 00:06:57,258
ツンツン、みたいな。ツンツンと思ってやってみたんじゃけれど
Like dipping my toes in... I thought I'd test the waters, but...

101
00:06:57,938 --> 00:07:02,168
さすがにちょっと怖いから次からメン限にしようと思ったのじゃ
As expected, it's a bit scary, so I thought I'd restrict it to member-only next time.

102
00:07:05,788 --> 00:07:07,498
変なこと言っていなかったっぽいけれど
It seems I didn't say anything weird, though.

103
00:07:08,578 --> 00:07:12,758
そう、変なこと言っていなかったっぽいけれど、次言わない保証がないのじゃ
Yeah, looks like I didn't say anything weird, but there's no guarantee I won't next time.

104
00:07:13,208 --> 00:07:22,098
から、次はちょっとあの安全地帯のお主らとね、メンバーシップの安全地帯のお主らと飲もうかな。うん、なんか閉じて、閉じてね
So next time, I think I'll drink with you guys in the safe zone—the membership safe zone. Yeah, keeping it private.

105
00:07:22,098 --> 00:07:26,548
何かあってもあのギリ許される環境で飲もうかなって思った
I thought I'd drink in an environment where even if something happens, it's barely forgivable.

106
00:07:28,478 --> 00:07:31,438
ちょっと、なかなか、なかなか難しかった
It was... quite, quite difficult.

107
00:07:32,798 --> 00:07:36,658
なんか笑いこと、笑いこと、笑い方とかもさ
Even the way I was laughing...

108
00:07:37,058 --> 00:07:40,408
なんか、あの、「ガハハ」って笑っちゃった
Like, I ended up laughing with a big "gahaha"!

109
00:07:40,858 --> 00:07:43,768
「ガハハハ」って笑っちゃったりさー
I was laughing like "Gahahahaha!" and stuff...

110
00:07:45,338 --> 00:07:47,788
なんかね、喉がね、かっぴらいてんだよね
You see, my throat was wide open.

111
00:07:48,068 --> 00:07:51,988
お酒飲むとね、呼吸が浅くなって、喉が結構開くから
When you drink alcohol, your breathing gets shallow and your throat opens up quite a bit...

112
00:07:53,078 --> 00:07:57,178
非常に声帯に悪い。喉に悪すぎるからね、やっぱ
It's extremely bad for your vocal cords. It's way too bad for the throat, after all.

113
00:07:57,888 --> 00:08:00,678
お酒はダメじゃの。お酒ダメじゃの
Alcohol is no good. Alcohol is no good.

114
00:08:01,078 --> 00:08:05,478
あの「ガハハ」って笑うとさ、楽しんだよ？楽しいから「ガハハハ」って笑うんじゃけれど
When you laugh with a "gahaha"—it's fun, okay? Because it's fun, I laugh "gahahaha," but...

115
00:08:06,128 --> 00:08:09,308
あのね、喉への負担がすごいのじゃ
You know, the strain on the throat is huge.

116
00:08:09,528 --> 00:08:11,838
面白いとね、あん笑っちゃうんじゃけれどね
When it's funny, I end up laughing like that...

117
00:08:13,808 --> 00:08:16,038
なかなかね、喉がびっくりしちゃう
It really takes your throat by surprise.

118
00:08:16,898 --> 00:08:17,828
笑い方じゃから
Because of that way of laughing.

119
00:08:20,738 --> 00:08:21,438
そう
Yeah.

120
00:08:22,018 --> 00:08:22,718
そうなんだよ
That's right.

121
00:08:22,718 --> 00:08:28,988
なら、あの、飲酒配信の次の日に歌枠入れたの大丈夫か？と思ってて
So I was like, "Is it really okay that I scheduled a singing stream the day after a drinking stream?"

122
00:08:30,298 --> 00:08:34,968
い、いけるか？わし、わしいけるか？って思ってたんだけど
Can... can I do this? Can I handle this? I wondered, but...

123
00:08:36,198 --> 00:08:37,078
歌うか
Shall I sing?

124
00:08:37,078 --> 00:08:39,738
歌うか、お主ら。歌歌うよ、歌歌うよ
Shall I sing, everyone? I'm gonna sing songs, I'm gonna sing!

125
00:08:39,958 --> 00:08:44,758
今日は、あ、今日歌う曲はね、あの、前回はボカロ縛りでやったんじゃけれど
Today, ah, the songs I'm singing today—last time I did only Vocaloid songs, but...

126
00:08:45,028 --> 00:08:48,818
今回はボカロ縛りではなく、あの色々歌おうと思ってて
This time it's not strictly Vocaloid, I'm planning to sing various songs.

127
00:08:49,008 --> 00:08:53,168
アニソンとかキャラソンとか、ボカロももちろん歌うんじゃけれど
Anison, character songs, and of course Vocaloid songs too...

128
00:08:55,108 --> 00:08:59,988
前さ、Twitterでさ、なんか「30選」みたいな
Before, on Twitter, I made a post like "30 selections"...

129
00:09:00,678 --> 00:09:06,918
30選、曲30選みたいなツイートを、した気がしていて
I feel like I tweeted something like "30 song selections".

130
00:09:07,458 --> 00:09:11,728
あんな中からもね、いくつかね、本当は歌いたい曲いっぱいあるんじゃけれど、そのカラオケ
From among those too, though there are actually so many songs I want to sing, the karaoke...

131
00:09:12,018 --> 00:09:18,968
今使わせていただいている、そのJOYSOUNDさんのね、カラオケアプリを使わせていただいて歌枠をしてるんだけど
I'm using the JOYSOUND karaoke app right now for this singing stream, but...

132
00:09:19,468 --> 00:09:23,958
その、そこに曲が入ってたやつ、入ってたやつは
The ones that were available in it...

133
00:09:24,088 --> 00:09:28,008
歌える！と思ったから、歌おうかなって思ってるのじゃ
I was like, "I can sing this!", so I'm thinking of singing them.

134
00:09:30,658 --> 00:09:31,548
そう
Yeah.

135
00:09:31,798 --> 00:09:36,008
なので、えー、まあどんな曲がくるかなと楽しみにつつ
So, um, while looking forward to what kind of songs are coming up...

136
00:09:37,478 --> 00:09:39,958
もうデビューしてちょっと経ったから
Since some time has passed since my debut...

137
00:09:40,488 --> 00:09:47,018
その最初の頃は、例えば、あの熱千めらだからサラマンダー聴きたいかなとか、メラ聴きたいかなとか
In the beginning, for example, since I'm Achichi Mela, I wondered if people wanted to hear Salamander or Mela...

138
00:09:47,388 --> 00:09:51,628
あの、こういう曲がたくさんの人に喜んでもらえるかな、みたいな
Like, "Would a lot of people be happy with songs like this?"

139
00:09:51,788 --> 00:09:59,908
わりとお主らのことを考えて、お主らのことを考えて、あの、どれなら喜んでくれるかな、と思って結構いっぱい選んだんじゃけれど
I thought a lot about you guys, considering what would make you happy, and picked a lot of them...

140
00:10:00,816 --> 00:10:03,496
ちょっと、ま、そろそろデビューして時間も経ってきたし
Well, it's been a while since my debut...

141
00:10:03,976 --> 00:10:09,336
なんか、今日... わしが歌いたいの歌うかーと思って
...so I thought today I'd just sing whatever I feel like singing!

142
00:10:09,936 --> 00:10:11,896
キャ、キャラソンとか入れちゃうかー？と思って
Like, maybe throwing in some character songs, too?

143
00:10:13,896 --> 00:10:18,416
ので、あのー、初めて聞く曲があるお主もね、もしかしたら居るかもしれないけど
So, um, there might be some of you hearing these songs for the first time...

144
00:10:18,536 --> 00:10:22,216
楽しんでいただけると嬉しいですのじゃ！ということで、歌枠始めるよ、お主ら！
...but I hope you enjoy them! So with that, I'm starting the karaoke stream, everyone!

145
00:10:24,416 --> 00:10:27,776
始める前に！「仮面外さないのー？」
Before starting! "Aren't you gonna take off your mask?"

146
00:10:27,976 --> 00:10:34,696
そうじゃよね、そうじゃよね、お主ら！あの、めらちゃんが可愛いお顔をお見せしながらね、見たいよね！
Right, right, everyone! You want to see Mela-chan showing her cute face while singing, right?

147
00:10:34,696 --> 00:10:39,136
お主ら、もう高評価は押してくれたかのー？押してくれた？
Have you all hit the like button yet? Did you hit it?

148
00:10:39,856 --> 00:10:44,936
もう押してくれた？わしは、いっぱいお主らに高評価押してほしいなー！
Did you hit it already? I really want you all to hit the like button a lot!

149
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:48,896
お願い、お願いなのじゃー！
Please, I'm begging you!

150
00:10:50,016 --> 00:10:55,616
ということで、歌うか！歌って、行くなっじょー！移動！
So, let me sing! Off to sing we go! Moving!

151
00:11:00,816 --> 00:11:04,616
あ！こっちにない！ないじょー！
Ah! It's not here! It's not here!

152
00:11:06,616 --> 00:11:09,136
ないじょー...
It's not here...

153
00:11:10,816 --> 00:11:14,936
待ってね。わし、どうやってイラスト入れたんだっけ？
Wait a sec. How did I put the illustration in back then?

154
00:11:19,416 --> 00:11:21,416
ちょっと待ってね、一回戻っていい？
Hold on a second. Can I go back for a bit?

155
00:11:23,016 --> 00:11:29,816
えーっと、コメントを出したくて、コメントをどうやって出していたか思い出せなくて... これコピーすればいいのかな？
Let's see, I wanted to show the chat comments, but I couldn't remember how I did it... Should I just copy this?

156
00:11:30,016 --> 00:11:33,736
コピー、移動、えーっと...
Copy, move, let's see...

157
00:11:33,736 --> 00:11:36,616
これ！ペースト！
This! Paste!

158
00:11:36,616 --> 00:11:39,256
これ！できた！
This! Done!

159
00:11:40,816 --> 00:11:41,896
よっし！
Alright!

160
00:11:42,256 --> 00:11:46,416
できたんじゃない？歌枠始められる！
Didn't I do it? Now I can start the karaoke stream!

161
00:11:46,416 --> 00:11:47,376
よっし！
Yes!

162
00:11:47,376 --> 00:11:53,376
それでは、歌枠始めます！今回のセトリもPNGで用意してまいりました！
So then, let's start the singing stream! I prepared the setlist as PNG images again!

163
00:11:53,376 --> 00:11:57,656
PNGで用意してきましたのじゃー！
I prepared them in PNG format!

164
00:11:57,896 --> 00:12:00,016
よいしょ、それでは！
Up we go, alright then!

165
00:12:00,016 --> 00:12:04,016
あー、あー、あー、あー...
Ah, ah, ah, ah...

166
00:12:04,016 --> 00:12:07,416
エコーをかけつつ、のじゃー！
Adding echo... noja!

167
00:12:07,416 --> 00:12:09,936
エコーかかってるー？
Is the echo working?

168
00:12:10,856 --> 00:12:13,416
お主ら、エコーかかってるー？
Everyone, is the echo working?

169
00:12:13,896 --> 00:12:15,336
どうー？
How is it?

170
00:12:16,016 --> 00:12:20,416
よいしょ、よいしょ、うん。
There we go, there we go, yep.

171
00:12:22,016 --> 00:12:25,056
始めていきますのじゃー！
Let me get started!

172
00:12:25,416 --> 00:12:28,936
それでは、1曲目...
So then, the first song...

173
00:12:29,616 --> 00:12:37,096
えー、「カワキヲアメク」って曲を歌います。歌いますのじゃ。
Um, I will sing a song called "Kawaki o Ameku". I'll sing it.

174
00:12:37,896 --> 00:12:42,616
えーっと... えーっと... あ！マイクがない！
Um... um... Ah! Where's my mic?!

175
00:12:46,416 --> 00:12:48,536
来た！マイク来た！
It's here! The mic is here!

176
00:12:48,816 --> 00:12:51,496
よし、行くなっじょー！よいしょ！
Alright, let's go! Here we go!

177
00:12:54,616 --> 00:12:59,056
いけるか...？いけた！
Will it work...? It worked!

178
00:13:08,856 --> 00:13:22,216
未熟　無情　されど　美しくあれ
Immature, heartless, yet remain beautiful...

179
00:13:29,816 --> 00:13:32,336
No Destiny　ふさわしくない
No Destiny, it's not fitting

180
00:13:32,336 --> 00:13:35,416
こんなんじゃきっと　物足りない
Like this, it's surely not enough

181
00:13:35,416 --> 00:13:37,816
くらい語っとけば　うまくいく
If I speak moodily like that, everything works out fine

182
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:41,816
物、金、愛、言、もう自己顕示欲く
Things, money, love, words... I'm sick of self-display

183
00:13:44,216 --> 00:13:49,016
既視感　何がそんな不満なんだ？　散々ワガママ語っといて
Déjà vu, what are you so dissatisfied about? After spouting so much selfishness...

184
00:13:49,016 --> 00:13:53,016
これ以上他に何がいる？　そんなところも　割と嫌いじゃない
What more do you need besides this? Even that part of you, I don't really hate it

185
00:13:57,016 --> 00:14:02,816
もう「聞き飽きたんだよ、そのセリフ。」　中途半端だけは嫌
"I'm sick of hearing that line." Anything half-hearted is what I hate

186
00:14:04,816 --> 00:14:07,416
もういい　ああしてこうして言ってたって
Enough already, even if you say do this and that

187
00:14:07,416 --> 00:14:10,016
愛してどうして言われたって
Even if you ask "Why?" when told to love

188
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:12,616
遊びだけなら簡単で　真剣交渉めちゃくちゃで
It's easy if it's just playing around, but serious relationships are a mess

189
00:14:12,616 --> 00:14:14,616
思いもしない軽い言葉
Thoughtless, light words...

190
00:14:14,616 --> 00:14:19,416
何度使い古すのか？
How many times will you wear them out?

191
00:14:19,416 --> 00:14:22,016
どうせ期待してたんだ　出来レースでも
I was expecting it anyway, even if it's a fixed race

192
00:14:22,016 --> 00:14:25,816
引用だらけのフレーズも　踵持ち上がる
Even with phrases full of quotes, my heels lift up

193
00:14:25,816 --> 00:14:33,816
言葉タブーにして　空気を読んだ　雨降らないでよ
Making words taboo, reading the room, don't let it rain

194
00:14:42,216 --> 00:14:44,516
そう、ドメカノの曲！
Yeah, the song from DomeKano!

195
00:14:47,816 --> 00:14:55,216
まどろっこしい話は嫌　必要最低限でいい
I hate roundabout talk, the bare minimum is fine

196
00:14:55,216 --> 00:15:00,024
2文字以内でどうぞ
Keep it within two characters, please

197
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:02,184
未完成だってどうぞ
Even if unfinished, go right ahead.

198
00:15:02,424 --> 00:15:09,324
紅の蝶は 向こうのメールも送らない
The crimson butterfly sends no messages from over there.

199
00:15:09,524 --> 00:15:16,424
脆い 扇子広げる その方が魅力的でしょう
Unfurling a fragile folding fan, isn't that far more alluring?

200
00:15:16,824 --> 00:15:21,624
迷えるくらいなら 去っといてくれ
If you're going to hesitate, just leave already.

201
00:15:21,824 --> 00:15:26,524
肝心なとこは筒抜けで 安心だけはさせられるような
When it matters most, you're transparent, giving me just enough peace of mind...

202
00:15:26,624 --> 00:15:31,524
甘い 雨が降れば 傘もしみなくなるだろう？
If a sweet rain falls, won't we stop needing an umbrella?

203
00:15:31,724 --> 00:15:34,224
このまま 期待したままのほうがよかった
It would've been better to stay expecting things like this.

204
00:15:34,324 --> 00:15:39,124
目を瞑った 変えたかった 大人ぶった 無くした 巻き戻せなかった
Closed my eyes, wanted to change, acted grown-up, lost it, couldn't rewind...

205
00:15:39,224 --> 00:15:43,724
今雨 止まないで
Right now, rain, please don't stop.

206
00:15:43,824 --> 00:15:48,324
コピー、ペースト、デリート
Copy, paste, delete...

207
00:15:48,524 --> 00:15:53,324
その繰り返し
Over and over again.

208
00:15:53,624 --> 00:15:57,624
吸って、吐いた
Inhaled, and exhaled.

209
00:15:58,224 --> 00:16:00,524
だから
That's why...

210
00:16:01,224 --> 00:16:05,524
それでもいいからさ 此処居たいよ
Even so, it's fine, so I want to stay here.

211
00:16:05,624 --> 00:16:09,424
ああしてこうして言ってたって 愛してどうして言われたって
Even if you say "do this, do that," even if you ask "why love me?"

212
00:16:09,524 --> 00:16:13,624
遊びだけなら簡単で 真剣交渉支離滅裂で
If it's just playing around, it's easy, but serious negotiations fall apart.

213
00:16:13,724 --> 00:16:19,224
思いもしない重い真実は タブーにしなくちゃな
Unexpected heavy truths must be made taboo, right?

214
00:16:19,424 --> 00:16:21,824
きっと 期待してたんだ
I must have been expecting something.

215
00:16:21,924 --> 00:16:27,724
出来レースでも 公式通りのフレーズも 踵上がる 癖も終わりにして
Even if it's a fixed race, or standard phrases, let's put an end to my habit of lifting my heels.

216
00:16:28,024 --> 00:16:34,724
空気を読んだ 空晴れないでよ
Reading the room, sky, please don't clear up.

217
00:17:05,824 --> 00:17:08,524
今日も 雨
Rain again today.

218
00:17:08,724 --> 00:17:11,824
傘を閉じて
Closing the umbrella,

219
00:17:12,024 --> 00:17:17,324
濡れて 帰ろうよ
let me head home getting wet.

220
00:17:19,624 --> 00:17:29,024
乾きを雨角でしたのじゃー！
That was "Kawaki o Ameku"!

221
00:17:29,824 --> 00:17:34,524
なんかこの曲さ、あの…
You know, this song... well...

222
00:17:35,324 --> 00:17:42,524
確か、出たて？リリースしたての時に、Twitterでめちゃくちゃバズってて…
I think around when it was first released, it went super viral on Twitter...

223
00:17:43,724 --> 00:17:47,324
Twitterで知ったんじゃけどね。
That's how I found out about it through Twitter.

224
00:17:48,324 --> 00:17:52,624
曲だけで…曲だけで好きになる…
Just the song itself... loving a song just for what it is...

225
00:17:53,624 --> 00:18:00,024
めちゃくちゃかっこいい曲、めちゃくちゃ引き込まれる曲でね、すごい好きなんのじゃ。
It's super cool and really captivating, so I love it so much.

226
00:18:00,624 --> 00:18:05,224
うん、すごい好き。だから歌っちゃった。
Yeah, I really love it. That's why I sang it.

227
00:18:05,724 --> 00:18:08,524
すごい好きな曲なんのじゃ。
It's a song I really love.

228
00:18:10,024 --> 00:18:13,024
そう、美波さん。美波さん…
Yeah, Minami-san. Minami-san...

229
00:18:13,224 --> 00:18:17,224
なんか、そう、この曲で美波さん知って、あの…
Like, yeah, I learned about Minami-san through this song, and...

230
00:18:19,224 --> 00:18:29,224
なんか近い時期に「ライラック」って曲？美波さんのね、「ライラック」って曲を聴いてね、それもねすごい好きになった。
Around that same time, I listened to a song called "Lilac" by Minami-san, and I fell in love with that one too.

231
00:18:29,324 --> 00:18:30,924
覚えあり。
I remember it well.

232
00:18:31,024 --> 00:18:33,424
そう。そうなんじゃ、漫画だけ知ってた。
Yeah. That's right, I only knew the manga before.

233
00:18:34,024 --> 00:18:37,424
やっぱ、あの、アニソンとかね、いろんな知る経緯があるのがいいよね。
You know, it's great how there are so many ways to discover anime songs and music in general.

234
00:18:37,724 --> 00:18:44,224
曲から…わしは曲から「あ、これアニソンだったんだ」って知るタイプが多いんじゃけど。
Starting from the song... I'm often the type who listens first and then realizes, "Oh, this was an anime song!"

235
00:18:44,324 --> 00:18:49,724
アニメで聴いたことあった、みたいのとか、アニメのCMとかで聴いたことあった、みたいの。
Or like, "I've heard this in an anime before," or "I heard this in an anime commercial."

236
00:18:50,024 --> 00:18:53,624
そういうのも多くてね、好きなんのじゃ。
I have a lot of those experiences too, which I really like.

237
00:18:54,024 --> 00:19:02,024
とか、アニソンとかね、キャラソンとかは特にね、その作品をね、知ってるとより楽しめる、みたいなさ、そういうのがあって。
Also, with anime songs or character songs in particular, knowing the anime series makes you enjoy the song even more.

238
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:08,524
その、より深まるからさ。わしはそういうのも面白いな、って思ってるんのじゃ。
Because it deepens the connection. I find that aspect really interesting.

239
00:19:08,624 --> 00:19:18,224
アニソンだけ知ってるのもある。わしはそれがすっごい…アニメは見てないけど曲だけ知ってる、みたいなのがすっごく多いんのじゃ。
There are also ones where I only know the anime song. For me, that happens a lot... like, I haven't watched the anime, but I know the song.

240
00:19:18,324 --> 00:19:19,424
そう、すっごく多い。
Yeah, that happens a whole lot.

241
00:19:19,524 --> 00:19:26,024
んー、入り口いっぱいあるとたくさんの人に曲聴いてもらえるし、いろんな人が知れるからいいよね。
Having many points of entry is great because more people get to hear the song, and people can discover new music.

242
00:19:26,124 --> 00:19:27,424
いいなって思うのじゃ。
I think that's really nice.

243
00:19:27,524 --> 00:19:29,824
商して、次の曲はこちら！
And now, here is the next song!

244
00:19:31,024 --> 00:19:33,424
これは…
This one is...

245
00:19:33,524 --> 00:19:38,224
あのさ、というかさ、わしさ、音ゲーのさ、話したよね。
Hey, wait, didn't I talk about rhythm games earlier?

246
00:19:39,024 --> 00:19:44,024
「ステラ」歌おうかなって思うんじゃけど…
I'm thinking of singing "Stella," but...

247
00:19:48,024 --> 00:19:52,224
わし…あれ？どこだ？
I... Huh? Where is it?

248
00:19:53,024 --> 00:19:55,724
どこだ？ステラ…え？待って？
Where is it? Stella... Huh? Wait.

249
00:19:56,524 --> 00:19:59,724
ちょっと待ってね。ちょっと待ってね。
Wait a second. Hold on a moment.

250
00:20:01,082 --> 00:20:02,542
ちょっと待ってね。
Hold on a second.

251
00:20:03,042 --> 00:20:04,052
おや？
Oh?

252
00:20:04,612 --> 00:20:05,552
おやおや？
Oh, dear...

253
00:20:06,042 --> 00:20:08,552
待って、わしカラ... カラオケないことある？
Wait, could it be... that I don't have the karaoke track?

254
00:20:09,142 --> 00:20:10,542
ごめん、確認... 確認しないで入れた。
Sorry, I added it without checking...

255
00:20:10,912 --> 00:20:13,282
確認しないで入れたの仕様ですが...
I put it in without checking, but...

256
00:20:14,572 --> 00:20:16,052
ないかも！
It might not be there!

257
00:20:16,542 --> 00:20:17,542
まずい！
Uh-oh!

258
00:20:17,812 --> 00:20:19,552
まずい、まずい、まずい！
This is bad, bad, bad!

259
00:20:20,552 --> 00:20:24,112
のー、のー、のーじゃー！
No... No... No-ja!

260
00:20:25,622 --> 00:20:27,552
まずい！
Oh no!

261
00:20:28,042 --> 00:20:30,042
絶対あるやろと思って入れたら...
I put it in assuming it'd definitely be there...

262
00:20:30,552 --> 00:20:33,052
え、嘘... 嘘じゃろ。ちょ、ちょ、ちょ...
Wait, no way... You gotta be kidding me. Wait, wait...

263
00:20:33,542 --> 00:20:34,852
な、ない？
Is it... not there?

264
00:20:36,042 --> 00:20:39,042
わしが使っているカラオケアプリに...
In the karaoke app I'm using...

265
00:20:39,542 --> 00:20:40,852
入って...
...it's not...

266
00:20:42,052 --> 00:20:44,052
いない可能性...
...included?

267
00:20:46,042 --> 00:20:47,042
のっ！
No!

268
00:20:47,542 --> 00:20:48,852
ちょ、あのさ...
Wait, hey...

269
00:20:49,242 --> 00:20:52,542
こ、今度歌わせて。ちゃんとカラオケ探してくるから。
L-Let me sing it next time. I'll properly look for the track.

270
00:20:53,042 --> 00:20:56,542
カラオケ、カラオケ探してくるから！ちょ、ちょ、ちょ...
I'll search for the karaoke track! Wait, wait, wait...

271
00:20:57,042 --> 00:20:59,542
な、なかったことにして！ちょっと待ってほしいのじゃ！
P-Pretend this didn't happen! Please give me a second!

272
00:21:00,042 --> 00:21:03,542
え、どうしよう... えっと... えっと...
What should I do? Um... Uh...

273
00:21:04,042 --> 00:21:06,542
でも、PNG... PNGにしてきちゃったから...
But I made it into a PNG... PNG overlay...

274
00:21:07,042 --> 00:21:08,542
一旦わしで隠して...
If I cover it with my avatar for now...

275
00:21:09,542 --> 00:21:11,252
え、わしで隠しても意味ない？
Wait, covering it with me doesn't help?

276
00:21:12,042 --> 00:21:13,542
はっ！
Ah!

277
00:21:14,042 --> 00:21:16,042
はっ、ちょ... え、お主等さ... お主等...
Ah, wait... Hey, everyone... Everyone...

278
00:21:16,542 --> 00:21:18,852
今一瞬だけ画面見ないでいてもらうことできる？
Can you look away from the screen for just a second?

279
00:21:19,042 --> 00:21:21,842
あのさ、今... 今見てるお主等さ...
Hey, right now... all of you watching...

280
00:21:22,042 --> 00:21:24,542
わしPNGで持ってきちゃったからさ...
Since I brought this as a static PNG...

281
00:21:25,042 --> 00:21:28,042
あの、そこだけ消すができなくてさ。あの...
I can't erase just that part. Um...

282
00:21:28,542 --> 00:21:31,042
ちょ、一瞬さ、目瞑ってもらっていい？
Hey, could you close your eyes for a moment?

283
00:21:31,242 --> 00:21:33,042
あの、セトリ全部バレちゃう。
All of the setlist will be spoiled.

284
00:21:33,142 --> 00:21:36,042
セトリ全部バレちゃうから、一瞬お主等目瞑ってもらっていい？
The whole setlist will be spoiled, so could you guys close your eyes for a second?

285
00:21:36,542 --> 00:21:38,542
行くよ？ 瞑っててね。行くよ！
Ready? Keep them closed, okay? Here I go!

286
00:21:39,042 --> 00:21:40,542
ステラあった？
Was Stella actually there?

287
00:21:40,842 --> 00:21:43,842
わしが使ってるねアプリにはね、なかったんだよね。
It wasn't in the app I'm using, you see.

288
00:21:44,242 --> 00:21:47,842
な... え、ちょ、もう一回見るか。気のせいだったら嫌だからな。
Is it... Wait, let me check again. I don't want it to just be a mistake.

289
00:21:49,042 --> 00:21:52,542
気のせいだったら嫌だから... じゃ、ちょっと目開けていいよ。今いいよ。
Just in case it was a mistake... Okay, you can open your eyes now. It's okay now.

290
00:21:53,042 --> 00:21:55,842
今目開けていいよ... ないな。ないな。
You can open your eyes now... Nope, it's not there. Not there.

291
00:21:57,542 --> 00:21:59,042
ないよね。
It really isn't, right?

292
00:22:00,042 --> 00:22:00,842
はい。
Yeah.

293
00:22:01,842 --> 00:22:03,242
そうし...
So...

294
00:22:04,042 --> 00:22:07,542
え、カタカナだよ、カタカナ。カタカナだよ、カタカナ。
Wait, it's in Katakana! Katakana, Katakana.

295
00:22:09,542 --> 00:22:10,542
うん。
Yeah...

296
00:22:10,842 --> 00:22:14,042
なかった！ガチでごめん！ガチでごめん、ガチでごめん！
It wasn't there! I'm so sorry! I'm really, really sorry!

297
00:22:14,542 --> 00:22:17,042
ど、土下座ごめん。土下座ごめん。
A-Apologies in dogeza! Apologies in dogeza!

298
00:22:17,542 --> 00:22:19,542
えっと... どうしようかな。
Um... What should I do?

299
00:22:20,542 --> 00:22:22,542
目瞑っててね！今、お主等！
Keep your eyes closed! Everyone, right now!

300
00:22:23,042 --> 00:22:25,542
いい？ 目瞑るよ？ 目瞑るよ？
Ready? Close your eyes! Close your eyes!

301
00:22:26,542 --> 00:22:28,042
目瞑るよ！
Close your eyes!

302
00:22:28,542 --> 00:22:31,042
行くよ？ 行くよ！
Here I go! Here I go!

303
00:22:31,242 --> 00:22:32,042
えー...
Uh...

304
00:22:33,242 --> 00:22:36,542
さ、さ、さ、ちょっとこれ、こ、こう隠して... こう隠して... よしよしよしよし。
Now, now, now... Let me hide it like this... hide it like this... Okay, okay, okay.

305
00:22:37,042 --> 00:22:38,542
ん？ 違うの... あ、やばい。
Huh? No... Ah, oh crap.

306
00:22:39,042 --> 00:22:41,542
こうして... こう、こう、こう、こう... よしよしよしよしよし。
Do this... like this, this, this... Okay, okay, okay, okay.

307
00:22:42,042 --> 00:22:44,042
目開けていいよー！
You can open your eyes now~!

308
00:22:44,242 --> 00:22:46,042
目開けていいよ、お主等！
You can open your eyes now, everyone!

309
00:22:47,042 --> 00:22:48,042
目開けていいよ。
Open your eyes.

310
00:22:48,542 --> 00:22:50,042
よしよしよしよしよし。
Alright, alright, alright.

311
00:22:50,542 --> 00:22:53,042
はいはいはいはい。行けた、行けた、行けた！
Yes, yes, yes, yes. Managed it, managed it!

312
00:22:53,542 --> 00:22:55,542
行けた、行けた。ちょ、ちょ、ちょ、ちょ...
Managed it, managed it. Wait, wait, wait...

313
00:22:55,842 --> 00:22:57,042
ふぅー、危なかったー！
Whew, that was close!

314
00:22:57,242 --> 00:22:58,542
え、どうしよう。本当は...
What should I do? Truth is...

315
00:22:59,242 --> 00:23:03,042
あの、30曲の中に入れてたステラを歌おうとしたんじゃけど...
I was going to sing Stella, which was among the 30 candidate songs...

316
00:23:03,542 --> 00:23:05,542
ちょっとオケが長... ちょ、これ本当にわしの準備不足だ。
But the karaoke track was... Wait, this is really my lack of preparation.

317
00:23:06,042 --> 00:23:07,542
わしの準備不足だ。
It's my fault for being unprepared.

318
00:23:08,542 --> 00:23:12,542
わしの準備不足で... あの、なかったので、ちょ、1曲プロセカの曲歌うか！
Due to my lack of prep... since it wasn't there, let me sing a Project SEKAI song instead!

319
00:23:13,042 --> 00:23:15,042
違うプロセカの曲歌うか。
Should I sing a different Project SEKAI song?

320
00:23:15,542 --> 00:23:18,042
違うプロセカの曲歌うか。
I'll sing a different Project SEKAI song.

321
00:23:19,542 --> 00:23:22,542
1曲違うプロセカの曲歌うのじゃ。
I'm gonna sing a different song from Project SEKAI.

322
00:23:23,042 --> 00:23:26,542
そう、なんかこれ歌おうかなと思ったんだけど...
Yeah, I thought about singing this one earlier...

323
00:23:27,042 --> 00:23:29,542
ステラ、ステラの方歌おうかなと思ってやめたやつがあって...
But I opted for Stella instead back then...

324
00:23:30,042 --> 00:23:32,042
や、やめたやつ！
The one I held back on!

325
00:23:32,242 --> 00:23:33,542
そう、そっち歌うから、うん。
Yeah, I'll sing that one instead, yep.

326
00:23:36,042 --> 00:23:37,042
うん、歌うのじゃ。
Yeah, I'll sing it.

327
00:23:37,542 --> 00:23:41,542
えっと、ちょっとセトリに書けないから...
Um, I can't write it on the setlist graphic right now...

328
00:23:42,542 --> 00:23:46,042
えー... うん、ごめんね。わちゃわちゃしちゃって。
Um... Sorry for all the fluster!

329
00:23:46,542 --> 00:23:49,042
本当にごめんね、お主等。まったく...
I'm really sorry, everyone. Jeez...

330
00:23:49,242 --> 00:23:51,542
まったくね、困っちゃつのじゃ。
Goodness, this is trouble, no-ja.

331
00:23:52,042 --> 00:23:53,042
えっと...
Um...

332
00:23:55,842 --> 00:23:56,842
あ、カタカナ。
Ah, katakana.

333
00:23:57,242 --> 00:23:58,242
えー...
Uh...

334
00:24:00,042 --> 00:24:01,842
よいしょ。よいしょ。
There we go. There we go.

335
00:24:02,042 --> 00:24:05,542
はいはいはいはいはいはいはいはい。
Alright, alright, alright.

336
00:24:06,042 --> 00:24:09,542
ちょ、1枚だけちょっと文字色が違うんだけど我慢してね。
Just one line has a different text color, but please bear with it.

337
00:24:10,542 --> 00:24:14,542
1枚だけ... 1枚だけね... あの、違うんだけどね。まぁ、気になる方は...
Just one line... Just one line is different. Well, for those who mind...

338
00:24:15,042 --> 00:24:18,542
A型のみなさんは気になるかな？ A型のみなさんは気になるかもしれないんだけど...
Type A people might notice? Type A folks might mind it, but...

339
00:24:21,042 --> 00:24:22,042
はい！
Okay!

340
00:24:22,242 --> 00:24:25,542
ちょっとじゃあ、あの... プロセカの...
Well then, let's see... A Project SEKAI...

341
00:24:26,042 --> 00:24:28,542
書き下ろし曲1曲歌おうかなと思って...
...commissioned song, I'll sing one!

342
00:24:29,042 --> 00:24:30,542
歌うのじゃ！
I'm gonna sing it!

343
00:24:32,042 --> 00:24:36,542
えっと... サイバーパンクデッドボーイ！
Um... Cyberpunk Dead Boy!

344
00:24:37,542 --> 00:24:38,542
うん。
Yeah.

345
00:24:39,042 --> 00:24:44,042
なんかね、ステラとね、サイバーパンクデッドボーイをね、書いた記憶あり。
I recall noting down both Stella and Cyberpunk Dead Boy...

346
00:24:44,242 --> 00:24:46,542
あの30曲のやつに。
...in that list of 30 candidate songs.

347
00:24:46,842 --> 00:24:49,042
すごい好きなのじゃ。めっちゃかっこいい。
I love it so much. It's super cool.

348
00:24:49,242 --> 00:24:53,042
めっちゃ... あ！ 左下がサイバーパンクデッドボーイになってる！
Super... Ah! The bottom-left setlist text says Cyberpunk Dead Boy!

349
00:24:53,242 --> 00:24:55,542
助けてお主等、どうしよう！
Save me everyone, what should I do?!

350
00:24:55,842 --> 00:24:57,242
元々なんて書いたっけ？
What did it originally say there?

351
00:24:57,542 --> 00:25:00,042
ちょ、待って... 歌、歌... 歌部分の...
Wait... Song, song... The song portion...

352
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:02,170
ん？歌唱部分...
Huh? Singing part...

353
00:25:02,170 --> 00:25:04,170
助けて！
Save me!

354
00:25:04,170 --> 00:25:08,420
歌唱部分の... 切り抜きは... 切り抜きは禁止なのじゃとか...
"Clips of... the singing parts... are prohibited," or something like that...

355
00:25:08,420 --> 00:25:11,790
なのじゃー... 待って！
...or something! Wait!

356
00:25:16,020 --> 00:25:17,420
こうか！
Like this!

357
00:25:19,020 --> 00:25:23,270
助けて面白！わし歌歌いたいのに... わし... わし...
Help, this is hilarious! I just want to sing... I... I...

358
00:25:23,270 --> 00:25:26,580
わし歌歌いたくてここに来たのに... よく気づいたね。
I came here because I wanted to sing... Good job noticing that.

359
00:25:27,010 --> 00:25:32,480
はいはいはい。あ、いけた！いいんじゃない？わし来た！わしいけるわ。ごめんおぬしら。
Alright. Oh, I got it! Isn't this good? I got it! I can do this. Sorry, guys.

360
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:36,580
わしすごいかも！わしできたかも！全部理解した。ほら！
I might be amazing! I might have done it! I understand everything now. Look!

361
00:25:36,820 --> 00:25:40,020
文字の色とかもほら、合わせられちゃうかも。
Look, I can even match the text colors.

362
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:42,100
はい、神！
Yes, I'm a genius!

363
00:25:42,100 --> 00:25:46,100
よしよしよしよし。ふー、危なかった！何事もなかったな。何事もなかった。
Alright, alright. Whew, that was close! Nothing happened. Nothing happened at all.

364
00:25:46,100 --> 00:25:50,440
最初から本日は『サイバーパンクデッドボーイ』を歌うつもりになった。
From the very beginning, I intended to sing "Cyberpunk Dead Boy" today.

365
00:25:50,440 --> 00:25:52,520
本当か？行くなじゃー！
Really? Let me go!

366
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:57,730
ちょ、飲酒してない！飲酒してない！飲酒してないって！抜けたって、酒！大丈夫なのじゃ。
Wait, I haven't been drinking! I haven't! I haven't been drinking! The alcohol wore off! It's fine.

367
00:25:58,300 --> 00:26:03,530
やばい！まだ1曲しか歌ってない！いつもなら、いつもならもう3、4曲歌ってる時間なのに！
Oh no! I've only sung one song! Usually... usually I'd have sung 3 or 4 songs by now!

368
00:26:03,530 --> 00:26:05,220
まずい！
This is bad!

369
00:26:06,040 --> 00:26:10,860
よし、大丈夫。大丈夫、大丈夫。よしよしよし。
Okay, it's fine. It's fine, it's fine. Alright, alright.

370
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:15,220
そしてBGMを切って、えー、エコーをかけて... はいはいはいはい。
And then I'll turn off the BGM, add some echo... Right, right, right.

371
00:26:15,220 --> 00:26:16,930
酔ってないって！
I'm not drunk!

372
00:26:19,020 --> 00:26:22,460
酔ってないって。え？でも元々『サイバーパンクデッドボーイ』を歌うつもりがなかったから...
I'm not drunk. Huh? But since I didn't plan on singing "Cyberpunk Dead Boy" originally...

373
00:26:22,460 --> 00:26:27,740
上手に歌える自信は... ちょ、言い訳ダサい！言い訳ダサいなのじゃ！行くなじゃー！
I'm not sure if I can sing it well... Wait, that excuse is lame! That excuse is so lame! Let me go!

374
00:26:29,840 --> 00:26:32,440
言い訳ダサいなのじゃ！
What a lame excuse!

375
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:35,840
やばいぞ。行くなじゃん。
Oh boy. Let's go.

376
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:52,040
お書きになったそんな音楽は現在使われておりません。もう一度お書き直しください。意味わかんねぇ！
The song you wrote is currently not in use. Please rewrite it again. That makes no sense!

377
00:26:57,140 --> 00:26:59,240
意味わかんねぇ！
Makes no sense!

378
00:27:04,240 --> 00:27:10,540
どーせ誰も聴いてなんかいないさ 音楽なんて全部ファッション 音楽なんて選手退場
Nobody is listening anyway. Music is all just fashion, a athlete leaving the field.

379
00:27:10,540 --> 00:27:16,840
どーせ何も伝えてなんかいないさ なんとなくトラック買っといて売名 あんな気取っておいて最低じゃない？
Nothing is being conveyed anyway. Buying tracks for fame, isn't acting all high and mighty the worst?

380
00:27:16,840 --> 00:27:22,840
どうしたん？ってどう見たって商売達でも大渋滞 それでもあっちこっちそっちぽっち卍 Z世代も欲しがる
"What's wrong?" No matter how you look at it, even commercial artists are jammed up. Still, here, there, Gen Z wants it too.

381
00:27:22,840 --> 00:27:28,940
パンチライン欲しいの 意味とかどっちだっていいよ 歌詞とかどうでもいいので乗れるの下さい
They want a punchline. Meaning or whatever doesn't matter. Lyrics don't matter, just give us something to groove to.

382
00:27:28,940 --> 00:27:35,040
さぁ皆で笑いましょう 芸術より数の大小 ヴァイラスに泣いた代償 じゃあどうすんの？
Come on, let me tell you, let's all laugh together. Quantity over art, the price paid to the virus. So what are you gonna do?

383
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:44,240
それでいいんだっけ 頭は空回り死んでいく
Is that really okay? My mind spins in circles and dies.

384
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:51,940
ふざけるな バイバイバズメロディ 疑えよ大概嘘ばかり
Don't mess around! Bye-bye buzz melody. Doubt it, it's mostly lies anyway.

385
00:27:51,940 --> 00:27:58,040
負けんな 幻想でも理想でもいい 君の歌いたかった物は何？
Don't lose. Whether fantasy or ideal, it's fine. What was it you wanted to sing?

386
00:27:58,040 --> 00:28:04,140
ぶざまでもオーライ 嘘じゃない お金や偽善で満たす前に
Even if it's ungraceful, it's alright, it's not a lie. Before filling yourself with money or hypocrisies...

387
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:11,840
負けんな 覚醒せよ鼓動たちよ 君の伝えたかった物は何？意味わかんねぇ！
Don't lose! Awaken, you heartbeats! What was it you wanted to convey? Makes no sense!

388
00:28:13,940 --> 00:28:17,640
ガチでここ... この曲の1番エロい場所ここ！
Seriously... the sexiest part of this song is right here!

389
00:28:17,640 --> 00:28:22,240
ガチカッコいい！ガチでカッコいい！ガチでありがとう！
Seriously cool! Seriously cool! Thank you so much!

390
00:28:24,040 --> 00:28:30,040
お書きになったそんな音楽は現在使われておりません。ポップソング、ヒットソング聴いてもう一度お書き直しください。あーもう、ハイカラお作法ばっか煩わしいわ。
The music you wrote is currently not in use. Listen to pop songs and hit songs and rewrite it. Ah geez, all these trendy manners are so annoying.

391
00:28:32,440 --> 00:28:36,040
はぁ、どいつもこいつもそいつもあいつも... 意味わかんねぇ！
Sigh, every single one of them... Makes no sense!

392
00:28:36,040 --> 00:28:41,840
どうしたん？ってどう見たって商売達でも大渋滞 それでもあっちこっちそっちぽっち卍 Z世代も欲しがる
"What's wrong?" No matter how you look at it, even commercial artists are jammed up. Still, here, there, Gen Z wants it too.

393
00:28:41,840 --> 00:28:48,040
パンチライン欲しいの 意味とかどっちだっていいよ 歌詞とかどうでもいいので伸びるの下さい
They want a punchline. Meaning or whatever doesn't matter. Lyrics don't matter, just give us something that goes viral.

394
00:28:48,040 --> 00:28:54,040
さぁ皆で祓いましょう 芸術より数なんでしょう？ ヴァイラスに詰んだ代償 じゃあどうすんの？
Come on, let's exorcise it all together. It's quantity over art, right? The price for getting cornered by the virus. So what are you gonna do?

395
00:28:54,040 --> 00:29:03,240
それでいいんだっけ？ 頭は空回り死んでいく
Is that really okay? My mind spins in circles and dies.

396
00:29:05,140 --> 00:29:11,240
ふざけるな バイバイバズメロディ 疑えよ大概嘘ばかり
Don't mess around! Bye-bye buzz melody. Doubt it, it's mostly lies anyway.

397
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:17,340
負けんな 幻想でも理想でもいい 君の歌いたかった物は何？
Don't lose. Whether fantasy or ideal, it's fine. What was it you wanted to sing?

398
00:29:17,340 --> 00:29:23,440
このままじゃ到底終われない 欲しいのはきっと金じゃない
We can't end it like this. What we want surely isn't money.

399
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:30,540
負けんな 覚醒せよ鼓動たちよ 君の歌いたかった歌がきっとあるんだ
Don't lose! Awaken, you heartbeats! There's surely a song you wanted to sing!

400
00:29:30,540 --> 00:29:37,740
ふざけるな！ふざけるな バイバイバズメロディ 疑えよ大概嘘ばかり
Don't mess around! Don't mess around! Bye-bye buzz melody. Doubt it, it's mostly lies anyway.

401
00:29:37,740 --> 00:29:43,840
負けんな 幻想でも理想でもいい 君の歌いたかった物は何？
Don't lose. Whether fantasy or ideal, it's fine. What was it you wanted to sing?

402
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:49,940
ぶざまでもオーライ 嘘じゃない お金や偽善で満たす前に
Even if it's ungraceful, it's alright, it's not a lie. Before filling yourself with money or hypocrisies...

403
00:29:49,940 --> 00:29:59,040
負けんな 覚醒せよ鼓動たちよ 君の伝えたかった物は何？意味わかんねぇ！意味わかんねぇよ！
Don't lose! Awaken, you heartbeats! What was it you wanted to convey? Makes no sense! Makes no sense!

404
00:30:00,048 --> 00:30:01,548
ああー！
Ahhh!

405
00:30:21,848 --> 00:30:24,248
意味わかんねぇ！
It makes no sense!

406
00:30:26,548 --> 00:30:28,148
やーん！
Yaan!

407
00:30:28,548 --> 00:30:30,848
かっこよくて笑った、『サイバーパンクデッドボーイ』。
"Cyberpunk Dead Boy" was so cool, I loved it!

408
00:30:30,948 --> 00:30:33,848
『サイバーパンクデッドボーイ』でしたのじゃー！
That was "Cyberpunk Dead Boy"!

409
00:30:33,948 --> 00:30:36,848
わしこの曲かっこよくて大すき！
I love this song, it's so cool!

410
00:30:37,848 --> 00:30:40,348
めちゃくちゃかっこいい曲！
It's an insanely cool song!

411
00:30:40,448 --> 00:30:43,948
やっぱね、わしね、わしがね...
You know, for me...

412
00:30:43,948 --> 00:30:47,348
好きな曲いっぱいあるんじゃけど、特に...
I have so many favorite songs, but especially...

413
00:30:47,348 --> 00:30:51,548
かっこいい曲を可愛い声の女の子が歌うキャラソンが大好きで。
I really love character songs where a girl with a cute voice sings a super cool song.

414
00:30:52,048 --> 00:30:54,048
んで、まあ、ワンダショの...
And, well, Wonderlands x Showtime's...

415
00:30:54,048 --> 00:30:55,748
曲？
song...

416
00:30:55,848 --> 00:30:57,648
ワンダショ書き下ろし曲じゃから...
Since it's a song written for Wonderlands x Showtime...

417
00:30:57,748 --> 00:31:00,248
もちろん男性ももちろん歌唱してるんじゃけど...
Of course the male characters sing it too, but...

418
00:31:00,348 --> 00:31:04,748
あのね、プロセカのエムちゃんってキャラの声がすっごいキュルキュルで可愛くて！
You know, Project Sekai's Emu-chan has such a high-pitched, cute character voice!

419
00:31:04,848 --> 00:31:10,548
キュルキュルで可愛い子がね、このちょっと治安悪めのね...
Having such a cute character sing this slightly edgy...

420
00:31:10,548 --> 00:31:16,848
ジャカジャカしたかっこいい曲を可愛く歌うのがめっちゃ好き！
rocking, cool song in a cute way—I love that so much!

421
00:31:16,948 --> 00:31:19,448
めっちゃ好きですのじゃ。
I really, really love it.

422
00:31:20,248 --> 00:31:21,548
自分も可愛い歌？
Did you sing cute yourself?

423
00:31:21,548 --> 00:31:23,048
ん？わしも可愛いよ？
Hm? I'm cute too, right?

424
00:31:23,048 --> 00:31:26,548
わしら...わしも可愛い？
Am I... Am I cute too?

425
00:31:27,548 --> 00:31:29,848
え、そう、同様の理由で...
Yeah, for that exact same reason...

426
00:31:29,948 --> 00:31:33,248
あの、以前『ミスコンダクター』が好きって話をしたことがあると思うんじゃけど...
I think I mentioned before that I like "Mr. Showtime"...

427
00:31:33,348 --> 00:31:37,448
かっこいい曲を可愛いボーカルの女の子が歌うのが大好きじゃから...
I love it when a girl with cute vocals sings a cool song...

428
00:31:37,548 --> 00:31:42,048
だから『ミスコンダクター』って曲の、あれ、複数人が歌唱してるバージョンがあるんじゃけど...
That's why for "Mr. Showtime", there's a version sung by multiple people...

429
00:31:42,148 --> 00:31:44,848
中でも黄っ子が歌唱してるのが好きな理由は...
And the reason I like the version sung by the yellow girl the most...

430
00:31:44,948 --> 00:31:47,848
可愛い女の子が歌ってるのが好きだからなんのじゃ。
is simply because I love hearing a cute girl sing it.

431
00:31:48,848 --> 00:31:50,048
ちょっと早口になっちゃった。
I started talking pretty fast.

432
00:31:50,848 --> 00:31:54,048
ちょ、ちょっと早口になっちゃったか？
Did... did I talk a bit too fast?

433
00:31:54,148 --> 00:31:57,448
まあそういうこともね、あるよね。
Well, that happens sometimes too, right?

434
00:31:57,648 --> 00:32:01,348
そう、この曲は原曲者さんも歌ってたり歌ってる版があったり...
Yeah, for this song, the original creator sang a version too...

435
00:32:01,448 --> 00:32:05,548
ボカロ版もあったりして、いろんなのがあるんじゃけど...
and there's a Vocaloid version, so there are various versions...

436
00:32:06,048 --> 00:32:09,648
そう、中でも書き下ろし版も結構わし好きなのよね。
Yeah, but I really like the newly commissioned game version too.

437
00:32:13,048 --> 00:32:15,848
のじゃ。早口トーク言っちゃった。
I ended up rambling fast.

438
00:32:18,048 --> 00:32:19,848
早口オタク君出ちゃった。
My fast-talking otaku mode came out.

439
00:32:20,048 --> 00:32:21,048
それでは...
Well then...

440
00:32:28,048 --> 00:32:30,048
ちょっと待ってね。ん？どうなってるんだ？
Wait a moment. Hm? What's going on?

441
00:32:32,048 --> 00:32:33,848
ん？ほうか。
Hm? Ah, I see.

442
00:32:37,048 --> 00:32:40,848
白...白...なるほどこうなってんのね。了解。
White... white... I see, so that's how it is. Got it.

443
00:32:41,248 --> 00:32:43,048
よし！よしよしよし...
Alright! Alright, alright, alright...

444
00:32:43,148 --> 00:32:46,048
ちょっとPNGをね、ちょっとだけ表示させた。
I displayed the PNG image for just a moment.

445
00:32:46,548 --> 00:32:48,848
これで行くか。これでいいか。行けるか。
Let's go with this. Is this okay? Will this work?

446
00:32:49,048 --> 00:32:51,548
辻褄が合うか。
Does everything line up properly?

447
00:32:51,648 --> 00:32:53,048
もうちょい上か？
A bit higher up?

448
00:32:53,148 --> 00:32:54,648
こんなもんか。
Something like this?

449
00:32:55,048 --> 00:32:57,848
というわけで！次の曲！
So then! The next song!

450
00:32:57,948 --> 00:33:01,848
歌っていこうと思うのじゃー！
Let's sing it!

451
00:33:02,048 --> 00:33:04,048
えっと、えっと...
Um, let's see...

452
00:33:04,548 --> 00:33:08,548
そう！なんとね、わしの、わしの大好きなね...
That's right! Surprisingly, my... one of my favorite songs...

453
00:33:08,648 --> 00:33:10,948
『-Across the line-』がね...
"-Across the line-"...

454
00:33:11,048 --> 00:33:16,848
JOYSOUND...カラオケ配信ストリーマーJOYSOUNDに入ってたの！
JOYSOUND... it was added to the streamer karaoke catalog on JOYSOUND!

455
00:33:16,948 --> 00:33:17,848
入ってたの！
It was actually there!

456
00:33:17,948 --> 00:33:22,548
そう！わしの超大好きな...わしの超大好きな曲がね...
Yes! A song I absolutely love...

457
00:33:22,648 --> 00:33:25,048
なんと入ってたので！歌っちゃおうと思うのじゃ。
was available, so I'm gonna sing it!

458
00:33:25,548 --> 00:33:27,848
あの『中二病でも恋がしたい！』
From "Love, Chunibyo & Other Delusions!"

459
00:33:29,848 --> 00:33:34,548
の、映画かあれ？映画の曲か？
...was it the movie? A movie song?

460
00:33:35,848 --> 00:33:38,248
キャラソン？あれなんだ？挿入歌か？
A character song? What was it, an insert song?

461
00:33:38,348 --> 00:33:40,848
キャラソンじゃけど、あれなんて言う枠なんだろう？
It's a character song, but what category does it fall under?

462
00:33:42,548 --> 00:33:44,248
の曲！
That song!

463
00:33:44,548 --> 00:33:47,048
でございますのじゃ！
That's the one!

464
00:33:47,248 --> 00:33:51,648
よし！歌っちゃう...歌っちゃうのじゃー！
Alright! I'm gonna sing it!

465
00:33:51,848 --> 00:33:56,848
そう、ZAQさん、作詞どころかもう作曲もやってらっしゃるよ。
Yeah, ZAQ-san wrote the lyrics and composed it as well.

466
00:33:57,048 --> 00:34:00,848
てか『中二病でも恋がしたい！』の曲は...
Honestly, the songs from "Love, Chunibyo & Other Delusions!"...

467
00:34:00,948 --> 00:34:05,848
あのキャラソンとかも含めてかなり彼女がやっていている...これ全部やってるよね？
including character songs, she did so many of them... she did basically all of them, right?

468
00:34:06,048 --> 00:34:10,848
なんか劇伴以外やってる気がするけど、どうじゃろ？
I feel like she handled everything except the background score, but who knows?

469
00:34:12,048 --> 00:34:14,248
映画の劇中歌かな？
Maybe an insert song from the movie?

470
00:34:14,848 --> 00:34:17,048
歌いますのじゃー！
Here I go singing it!

471
00:34:18,548 --> 00:34:24,548
よし、BGM消して...エコーつけて...よし、行くのじゃ！
Alright, turning off BGM... turning on echo... okay, let me begin!

472
00:34:29,848 --> 00:34:35,548
[Title: -Across the line- / 小鳥遊六花(CV: 内田真礼) / 作詞・作曲 ZAQ]
[Title: -Across the line- / Rikka Takanashi (CV: Maaya Uchida) / Lyrics & Composition: ZAQ]

473
00:34:50,048 --> 00:34:55,048
眠る前に 抱きしめた
Before falling asleep, I held tight...

474
00:34:55,248 --> 00:35:00,048
あの枕に 君を重ねた後
...to that pillow, overlapping it with thoughts of you...

475
00:35:00,106 --> 00:35:02,056
あっと...
Ah...

476
00:35:02,156 --> 00:35:10,856
水平線の向こう側にいる 君の夢をみた
I dreamed of you beyond the horizon.

477
00:35:14,356 --> 00:35:19,856
根拠のない強さも 理由だらけの弱さも
Both groundless strength and weakness full of reasons...

478
00:35:20,056 --> 00:35:24,356
お互い抱きしめ合えたから
...we held each other tight through them all.

479
00:35:25,056 --> 00:35:33,256
あの頃の痛みは 風に乱れ散ったよ
The pain of those days scattered in the wind.

480
00:35:34,256 --> 00:35:37,356
向こう側に連れていって
Take me to the other side.

481
00:35:37,656 --> 00:35:43,756
愛しいから泣いた けど 愛しいからもっと笑った
I cried because I loved you, but smiled even more because I loved you.

482
00:35:44,056 --> 00:35:48,856
「いなくなる」と伝えるより 信じるほうが尊いな
Rather than saying "I'll disappear," believing is far more precious.

483
00:35:49,156 --> 00:35:55,756
今がどんどん重なって 君の日々を彩っていく
The present keeps building up, adding color to your days.

484
00:35:56,056 --> 00:36:00,856
私の存在は 何色をしてる？
What color is my existence?

485
00:36:00,956 --> 00:36:08,556
これは解けない魔法 「たぶんずっと好きだよ」を誓うね
This is an unbreakable spell; I swear "I'll probably love you forever."

486
00:36:19,356 --> 00:36:28,056
ノスタルジックな 心の核は いらない羽根で固まる
The nostalgic core of my heart hardens with unneeded wings.

487
00:36:31,056 --> 00:36:36,756
いくら探してみても 思いぶつけてみても
No matter how much I search, no matter how much I express my feelings...

488
00:36:37,056 --> 00:36:41,056
白さは屈折すると思ってた
...I thought whiteness would refract.

489
00:36:41,256 --> 00:36:49,856
予期しない場所から ふいに抱きしめられて
Suddenly embraced from an unexpected place...

490
00:36:51,256 --> 00:36:54,656
共鳴しあう出会い
...a resonant encounter.

491
00:36:54,856 --> 00:37:00,056
思い出したくない 景色ほど色あせずに残る
The scenes I want to forget remain without fading.

492
00:37:00,156 --> 00:37:06,156
恥ずかしくて会えないのに 君の名を呼んじゃうなあ
Even though I'm too embarrassed to meet you, I end up calling your name.

493
00:37:06,356 --> 00:37:13,556
無慈悲な直感が 導きだす二人の運命
A merciless intuition guides our destiny.

494
00:37:13,856 --> 00:37:18,056
弾ける効果音 閃くような未来
Popping sound effects, a flashing future.

495
00:37:18,256 --> 00:37:25,556
君の手を握ったよ なんだか笑顔まで似てきたね
I held your hand, and somehow even our smiles started to look alike.

496
00:37:47,356 --> 00:37:55,556
小さな部屋の扉あけて 大きな世界が泳いでる
Opening the door of a small room, a vast world swims.

497
00:37:55,856 --> 00:38:03,356
煌めく目を細める君 そっちの方に今行くね
You squint your sparkling eyes, I'm heading your way now.

498
00:38:03,556 --> 00:38:09,556
愛しいから泣いた けど 愛しいからもっと笑った
I cried because I loved you, but smiled even more because I loved you.

499
00:38:09,856 --> 00:38:14,856
「いなくなる」と伝えるより 信じるほうが尊いな
Rather than saying "I'll disappear," believing is far more precious.

500
00:38:15,056 --> 00:38:21,556
今がどんどん重なって 君の日々を彩っていく
The present keeps building up, adding color to your days.

501
00:38:21,856 --> 00:38:26,556
私の存在は 何色をしてる？
What color is my existence?

502
00:38:26,856 --> 00:38:34,556
これは解けない魔法 「たぶんずっと好きだよ」を誓うね
This is an unbreakable spell; I swear "I'll probably love you forever."

503
00:38:48,556 --> 00:38:54,056
のじゃ！-Across the line- でしたのじゃー！
Noja! That was "-Across the line-"!

504
00:38:56,056 --> 00:38:58,256
あのね コメント欄でバレてた
You know, people in the comments figured it out!

505
00:38:58,856 --> 00:39:04,556
あの 声優さんがね 内田真礼さんなんじゃけど 寄せてたのバレてた？
Um, the voice actress is Maaya Uchida... could you tell I was trying to imitate her voice?

506
00:39:05,256 --> 00:39:10,556
寄せて歌ってみたのじゃ！なんでかって 原曲が大好き！
I sang while imitating her! Why? Because I love the original song so much!

507
00:39:11,256 --> 00:39:14,356
-Across the line- が大好き！そう！そうそう！
I love "-Across the line-"! Yeah! Exactly!

508
00:39:14,556 --> 00:39:18,756
僕ね 実はね 歌っていてね それがね バレていた
To be honest, while I was singing, people noticed!

509
00:39:19,556 --> 00:39:21,556
バレてもいましたのじゃ
Yeah, you guys totally caught on!

510
00:39:22,256 --> 00:39:26,556
そうなんだよ わしさ 内田真礼さん好きでさ
That's right. I really love Maaya Uchida,

511
00:39:26,656 --> 00:39:33,256
この曲知ったのもね わしの曲を知る経緯って多分結構変
and how I found this song... my story of discovering songs is probably pretty weird.

512
00:39:33,856 --> 00:39:36,056
変なんだけど
It's weird, but...

513
00:39:36,556 --> 00:39:45,056
まず 内田真礼さんの 声優さんとしてではなく 声優アーティストとしての楽曲が好きだった
First of all, I loved Maaya Uchida's music not just as a voice actress, but as a voice actor-artist.

514
00:39:46,056 --> 00:39:50,056
そう なんか Smiling Spiral の話とかしたことあると思うんじゃけど
Yeah, I think I've talked about "Smiling Spiral" before,

515
00:39:50,256 --> 00:39:54,556
そう 内田真礼さんの アーティストとしての曲を聴いていた
so yeah, I was listening to Maaya Uchida's solo artist songs.

516
00:39:54,856 --> 00:39:55,856
んで
And then,

517
00:39:56,556 --> 00:40:00,056
そこから 内田真礼さんが声優として歌唱してるキャラ...
from there, character songs sung by Maaya Uchida as a voice actress...

518
00:40:00,124 --> 00:40:02,384
全部聴いていた中で
Among all the ones I listened to...

519
00:40:02,864 --> 00:40:06,164
えーっと 『Across the line』を見つける
...I found "-Across the line-".

520
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:10,484
「めっちゃいいやん 何だこの曲」と思う
I thought, "This is so good, what is this song?!"

521
00:40:10,784 --> 00:40:12,784
うんね わしが
And then, you know...

522
00:40:12,784 --> 00:40:19,484
あの すごい好きな作家さんの中にね ZAQさんがいて ZAQさんっていう作家さんがすごい好きなんじゃけど
ZAQ is one of my favorite composers. I really love the creator ZAQ,

523
00:40:19,484 --> 00:40:21,344
そこてZAQさんを知るの
and that was how I found out about ZAQ.

524
00:40:21,344 --> 00:40:22,144
そう
Yeah.

525
00:40:22,544 --> 00:40:27,824
内田真礼さんが歌ってるからで聴いたら 「なんじゃこの曲 めっちゃええ」と思って
I listened to it because Maaya Uchida was singing it, and I was like, "What is this song? It's amazing!"

526
00:40:28,064 --> 00:40:31,824
あの… そう 「なんだこの作詞作曲」と思って
And then I thought, "Who wrote and composed this?!"

527
00:40:32,204 --> 00:40:40,144
初めて歌を聴いてる時に 歌ってる人じゃなくて作ってる人に目を向け始めたのがここ
That was the first time I started paying attention to the creator rather than the singer when listening to a song.

528
00:40:40,384 --> 00:40:46,464
そう それまでは誰が作ってるかより 誰が歌ってるかで曲を聴くことの方が多かったんじゃけど
Before that, I usually listened to songs based on who was singing rather than who wrote them.

529
00:40:46,464 --> 00:40:47,524
そう
Yeah.

530
00:40:47,844 --> 00:40:53,704
ここて初めて作家さんの存在を意識して 意識して「ZAQさんってやべー」と思って
That was the first time I became aware of song creators, realized how amazing ZAQ was,

531
00:40:54,744 --> 00:41:03,504
ZAQさんの曲をこう 一覧て全部 とりあえすZAQさんが提供した曲は全部聴くみたいなのをし始めて
and started looking up all of ZAQ's songs on a list, listening to every single track she provided.

532
00:41:03,744 --> 00:41:15,064
そう たからそれこそみお先輩とかがさ 前のホロとり?てさ 『HOWLING』がさ…
Yeah, so for instance, Mio-senpai sang "HOWLING" during the Holo-Dori stream back then...

533
00:41:15,064 --> 00:41:17,384
…を知ったのも 彼女が提供していたからみたいな
...and I knew about that song because she was the one who provided it.

534
00:41:17,744 --> 00:41:25,784
感じ そう そこからね 作曲者さん 誰が作ったかをすごい意識するようになって
Yeah. From then on, I became super conscious of who composed the songs,

535
00:41:25,784 --> 00:41:31,844
彼女以外にも 他のアニソン作家さんたったりが 「この人 他にどういう曲書いてるんだろう」みたいのを聞くようになったのじゃ
and I started checking out other anime song composers, wondering what other songs they had written.

536
00:41:32,484 --> 00:41:33,284
そう
Yeah.

537
00:41:33,804 --> 00:41:42,404
たからわしが結構 曲を誰が作ったかを意識して聴き始めたきっかけの曲が『Across the line』て
So "-Across the line-" was the song that got me to start paying attention to who created the songs I listened to.

538
00:41:42,404 --> 00:41:46,804
『Across the line』があまりにも曲として好きすきて
I loved "-Across the line-" so much purely as a song...

539
00:41:47,444 --> 00:41:56,304
そこから… そこからわしの楽曲オタクが始まった
That's where... that's where my journey as a music otaku started.

540
00:41:57,544 --> 00:42:00,744
そこからわしの楽曲オタクが始まった
That's where my music otaku journey began.

541
00:42:02,884 --> 00:42:04,344
ということなんのじゃ
That's how it happened.

542
00:42:05,524 --> 00:42:11,844
たからわしはこの曲を先に聴いて そこから『中二病ても恋がしたい!』1期から見たっていう
So I actually listened to this song first, and then went back to watch season 1 of "Love, Chunibyo & Other Delusions!"

543
00:42:12,244 --> 00:42:17,964
順番か変なの 曲からアニメを見始めるみたいなことか多い子供たった
The order was completely reversed! I was a kid who often started watching an anime because of a song.

544
00:42:24,144 --> 00:42:27,824
始まりの曲なんのじゃ たから…
It was the song that started it all. So...

545
00:42:27,824 --> 00:42:35,124
映画の劇中歌か何かたと思って1期を見るみたいな
...I thought it was an insert song for a movie or something, so I went to watch season 1!

546
00:42:35,404 --> 00:42:39,164
そうそうそう アニメを見に行くみたいな感じたったのじゃ
Yeah, yeah, yeah! It felt like I was going to check out the anime itself.

547
00:42:39,904 --> 00:42:44,264
そうそうそうそう 内田真礼さんからのZAQさん分かるしろ?
Right, right! Going from Maaya Uchida to ZAQ makes total sense, right?

548
00:42:44,264 --> 00:42:51,164
内田真礼さんのアーティスト曲とかも結構ZAQさんか何曲か提供しておられたり
ZAQ has provided quite a few songs for Maaya Uchida's artist discography as well,

549
00:42:51,584 --> 00:42:54,744
関係性か結構あるから そこから入ったのじゃ
so they have a strong connection. That's how I got into it.

550
00:42:57,464 --> 00:43:07,564
たから割とね どの曲てもわしはあれかもね 曲の知リ方か変かも 変なことか多いかもしれない
So for almost any song, my way of discovering it might be a bit weird. I might have a lot of weird entry points.

551
00:43:08,584 --> 00:43:14,684
てむそういう色んな入り口かあるってすごい素敵なことたなーってわし思う
But I think having all these different entry points is a really wonderful thing.

552
00:43:15,084 --> 00:43:20,164
それこそVTuberさんも VTuberさんのオリジナル曲も結構わし聴くんたよ
Same with VTubers, I actually listen to a lot of VTubers' original songs too.

553
00:43:20,464 --> 00:43:32,464
たから「この曲いいな」みたいな 配信はあまり見たことないけむ「この人のこの曲いいな」みたいなのも結構何曲もあったリするのじゃ
I'll think, "Oh, this song is great," even if I haven't watched their streams much. I have quite a few songs like that!

554
00:43:34,884 --> 00:43:36,484
そうなんのじゃ
That's how it is.

555
00:43:38,964 --> 00:43:45,364
そして ちょっとしたお喋りをしたところて 次何じゃったかな
Now, after that little chat, what was next?

556
00:43:45,364 --> 00:43:47,444
あ! ボカロ来た!
Ah! A Vocaloid song is up!

557
00:43:47,444 --> 00:43:49,764
おぬしらボカロ来た!
Guys, Vocaloid is here!

558
00:43:49,764 --> 00:43:52,044
ボカロ聴きたかったんじゃないのおぬしら!
Weren't you guys wanting to listen to Vocaloid songs?!

559
00:43:52,264 --> 00:43:55,764
おぬしら最近わしか…
Lately, you guys...

560
00:43:56,944 --> 00:44:07,664
ボカロ以外を… 『サイバーパンクデッドボーイ』ボカロっつったらボカロか まぁボカロか 失礼いたしました
...haven't heard me sing much outside of— wait, is "Cyberpunk Dead Boy" considered Vocaloid? Well, I guess it is! My bad, my bad!

561
00:44:08,884 --> 00:44:15,284
ボカロ聴きたかったんじゃないと思って用意してきましたのじゃ
I thought you guys wanted to hear Vocaloid songs, so I prepared one!

562
00:44:15,284 --> 00:44:17,364
ナブナさんの『メリュー』
"Meryu" by n-buna!

563
00:44:17,544 --> 00:44:28,064
ナブナさんはあれたね ヨルシカとかの曲を作っていらっしゃる方 ヨルシカを始める前のボカロ名義というのカナ?
n-buna is the person who makes songs for Yorushika! Or should I say, his Vocaloid producer name before starting Yorushika?

564
00:44:28,844 --> 00:44:32,924
曲てすねっじゃ 歌うのじゃ!
Here's the song! Let's sing it!

565
00:44:33,944 --> 00:44:45,864
今のところ全部知らない? この歌枠はいつもはおぬしらか分かる目の曲をいっぱい用意してくるんじゃけむ 今日はかなり…
You don't know any of the songs so far? Usually for these singing streams, I prepare lots of songs you guys would know, but today is pretty...

566
00:44:46,064 --> 00:44:56,064
わしか「歌いたい!」って思ったの 相当 自己満足的なところアリを用意してきました!
...filled with songs I personally just really wanted to sing! I brought a pretty self-satisfying setlist today!

567
00:44:57,544 --> 00:45:00,136
から あの… なんたろう 知ってくれると…
So, um... I hope you get to know these songs...

568
00:45:00,142 --> 00:45:01,872
きっかけになるといいなー
I hope it serves as a catalyst.

569
00:45:01,972 --> 00:45:04,472
て思いましたー！よいしょー！
I thought to myself! Alright then!

570
00:45:05,172 --> 00:45:09,172
それでは、歌いますのじゃー！よいしょー！
Well then, I shall sing! Here we go!

571
00:45:09,672 --> 00:45:10,872
いけるか？
Ready for this?

572
00:45:12,072 --> 00:45:14,372
ん？ん。
Hmm? Yeah.

573
00:45:27,072 --> 00:45:35,072
夕陽が落ちる様に
Like the setting sun falling,

574
00:45:35,072 --> 00:45:41,572
胸が染まるので
As my chest is stained,

575
00:45:41,572 --> 00:45:49,072
耳鳴りのような
Like a ringing in the ears,

576
00:45:49,072 --> 00:45:56,572
鼓動を隠して
Hiding my heartbeat...

577
00:45:56,572 --> 00:46:00,072
バスに乗った僕は言う
Boarding the bus, I say:

578
00:46:00,072 --> 00:46:04,072
君は灰になって征く
"You are turning to ashes and going away."

579
00:46:04,072 --> 00:46:08,572
たとえばこんな言葉さえ
Even if words like these,

580
00:46:08,572 --> 00:46:12,572
失う言葉が僕に言えたら
Even if these parting words could be spoken by me...

581
00:46:12,572 --> 00:46:17,072
灯籠の咲く星の海に
Into the sea of stars where lanterns bloom,

582
00:46:17,072 --> 00:46:20,572
心臓を投げたのだ
I threw my heart.

583
00:46:20,572 --> 00:46:27,072
もう声も出ないそれは 僕じゃどうしようもなかったのだ
No voice comes out anymore—there was nothing I could do about it.

584
00:46:41,072 --> 00:46:48,572
悲しくもないし
I'm not sad,

585
00:46:48,572 --> 00:46:56,072
苦しくもないのに
Nor am I in pain,

586
00:46:56,072 --> 00:47:08,572
辛いと思うだけ
Yet I only feel it's painful...

587
00:47:08,572 --> 00:47:13,572
古びたバス停の端
At the edge of an old bus stop,

588
00:47:13,572 --> 00:47:17,572
傘を持った僕がいる
Standing here holding an umbrella,

589
00:47:17,572 --> 00:47:22,072
今でさえ埃を被った
Covered in dust even now...

590
00:47:22,072 --> 00:47:26,072
夜空の隅に足はつくのに
Though my feet touch the edge of the night sky,

591
00:47:26,072 --> 00:47:30,072
心臓が痛いから死んだふりの
Because my heart hurts, playing dead,

592
00:47:30,072 --> 00:47:34,072
毎日を見ないよ
I refuse to face each day.

593
00:47:34,072 --> 00:47:40,572
もういっそ死のうと思えたなら僕はこうじゃなかったのだ
If I could have just given up and died, I wouldn't have ended up like this.

594
00:47:55,572 --> 00:48:00,072
どうせ死ぬくせに
Even though we'll die anyway,

595
00:48:00,072 --> 00:48:03,572
辛いなんておかしいじゃないか
Isn't it ridiculous to complain that it hurts?

596
00:48:03,572 --> 00:48:07,572
どうせ死ぬくせに辛いなんて
Even though we'll die anyway, to feel pain...

597
00:48:07,572 --> 00:48:14,572
あぁ あぁ
Ah... Ah...

598
00:48:14,572 --> 00:48:22,072
だから愛さえないこんな世界の色に 僕の歌を混ぜて
So into the colors of this loveless world, blending my song...

599
00:48:22,072 --> 00:48:30,072
もうどうかしたいと想うくせに僕はどうもしないままで
Though wanting so desperately to do something, I remain doing nothing at all.

600
00:48:30,572 --> 00:48:33,572
あぁ
Ah...

601
00:48:33,572 --> 00:48:38,072
灯籠の咲く星の海に心臓を投げたのだ
Into the sea of stars where lanterns bloom, I threw my heart.

602
00:48:38,072 --> 00:48:42,572
もう声も出ないから死んだふりなんてどうもなかったのに
No voice comes out anymore, so playing dead was nothing to me, and yet...

603
00:48:42,572 --> 00:48:47,072
僕もきっとこうで良かったのに
I'm sure it would have been fine for me like this too, and yet...

604
00:48:47,072 --> 00:48:56,572
君がずっと遠く笑ったのだ
You smiled from so far away.

605
00:49:00,572 --> 00:49:07,572
メリューでしたのじゃー！
That was "Meryu"!

606
00:49:08,572 --> 00:49:19,572
なんか、前回わしが歌枠やったときに、すごいアップテンポなものが多くて...
You know, last time I did a singing stream, there were so many upbeat songs...

607
00:49:20,572 --> 00:49:26,572
アップテンポなものがめちゃくちゃ多かったから、ちょっとしっとりさせるかと思って...
Since there were so many high-tempo songs, I thought, "Let me add some calm, mellow vibes..."

608
00:49:27,572 --> 00:49:33,572
ちょっと、ちょっとしっとりめもお主ら欲しいんじゃないのー？って
I thought, "Surely you guys want a bit of a mellow mood too, right?"

609
00:49:34,572 --> 00:49:40,072
そう、ボカロロック多かったから。しっとりも欲しいんじゃないのお主らー？って思ったのじゃ。
Yeah, because there was a lot of Vocaloid rock before. So I figured, "Wouldn't you guys want something mellow too?"

610
00:49:41,072 --> 00:49:47,072
でも...でも、わしがお主らをただしっとりさせるわけなくて笑った。
But... but there's no way I'd just leave you guys in a quiet, mellow mood, which makes me laugh.

611
00:49:48,072 --> 00:49:54,072
しっとりたださせているつもりももちろんなく、そろそろいいですか？暴れて。
Naturally, I have no intention of just keeping things calm—is it alright if I start going wild soon?

612
00:49:55,072 --> 00:49:59,872
そろそろ、そろそろ暴れていいですか？
Is it alright if I... is it alright if I start going wild now?

613
00:50:03,280 --> 00:50:08,080
そろそろお主らもわしが暴れてるとこ聴きたいんでしょ？
You guys probably want to hear me go wild by now, right?

614
00:50:11,880 --> 00:50:13,580
暴れたいなと思って。
I thought I'd like to go wild too.

615
00:50:14,380 --> 00:50:17,580
いやね、ずっと好きって言ってたからね。
Well, I've been saying I love this for a long time.

616
00:50:18,480 --> 00:50:22,980
なんか聴きたかった人多いんじゃないかなって思って。
I thought a lot of people might have wanted to hear it.

617
00:50:23,580 --> 00:50:27,780
いやでも、やっぱ好きなのと上手に歌えるのとは違うんじゃよ。
But you know, liking a song and singing it well are two different things.

618
00:50:28,180 --> 00:50:32,080
なんか分かるじゃろ？お主らカラオケとかでさ、好きな曲歌ってもさ。
You know what I mean, right? Even when you sing your favorite songs at karaoke...

619
00:50:32,480 --> 00:50:36,580
なかなかさ、いや難しいな、この曲好きなんだけどな、みたいな。
It's often like, "Man, this song is so hard, even though I love it."

620
00:50:39,180 --> 00:50:41,280
あるじゃろ？
Right?

621
00:50:41,280 --> 00:50:47,880
あると思うの具体的、ちょっとあの、こんだけ言ってて、ちょっと触れないわけにはいかないなと思って持ってきた。
I think so, and after hyping it up this much, I felt like I just had to bring it today.

622
00:50:48,380 --> 00:50:49,880
で、で、で、で、で。
So, so, so, so...

623
00:50:50,580 --> 00:50:56,580
えーっと、あのわしが自己紹介動画とか色んなところで。
Um, in my self-introduction video and various other places...

624
00:50:56,880 --> 00:51:03,580
あの『SAKKAC CRAFT』っていうアルバムが、好きって話をずっとしておりまして。
I've been talking all along about how much I love the album "SAKKAC CRAFT".

625
00:51:04,780 --> 00:51:09,680
『SAKKAC CRAFT』が好きって話をっずっと言ってたんじゃけど、ちょっと曲が難しすぎて。
I kept saying I loved "SAKKAC CRAFT," but the songs are just way too difficult...

626
00:51:10,780 --> 00:51:18,880
ちょっとデビューして直後にちょっと難い曲を歌って振り回されてるのをちょっと見せるのちょっと申し訳ないなと思い。
So right after my debut, I felt a bit bad showing myself struggling and getting swung around by such tough songs...

627
00:51:21,580 --> 00:51:24,080
そう、ちょっとやっぱ難しい曲ってさ。
Yeah, hard songs are like that, right?

628
00:51:24,280 --> 00:51:27,580
あの、歌ってみたとかだったらまだしもさ、生でさ。
I mean, on a cover release it's one thing, but singing live...

629
00:51:27,680 --> 00:51:31,980
難しい曲歌うと結構なんじゃろ、聞いてて不安になるというかさ。
Singing a tough song live can make listeners feel a bit uneasy, right?

630
00:51:32,280 --> 00:51:36,880
「お、ま、歌枠だし、こんなもんかクオリティ」ってなっちゃうじゃろ？
You might end up thinking, "Well, it's just a live stream, so I guess this quality is expected," right?

631
00:51:37,080 --> 00:51:40,080
それをデビューした直後にやると良くないかなと思ったけど。
I thought doing that right after debut wasn't a good idea, but...

632
00:51:40,280 --> 00:51:43,080
まあさすがにもうデビューして2ヶ月。
Well, it's already been 2 months since my debut.

633
00:51:43,280 --> 00:51:49,080
2ヶ月経って、まあここまで今わしのことを見てくれてる人間たちは。
2 months have passed, and the people watching me up until now...

634
00:51:49,280 --> 00:51:53,080
きっとメラちゃんのことが大好き！なんじゃないの？お主ら。
...must really, really love Mela-chan! Right, everyone?

635
00:51:53,480 --> 00:51:57,980
お主らメラちゃんのこと大好きじゃから、まあ多少の難しさには目を瞑ってくれるかなと。
Since you all love Mela-chan so much, I thought you'd turn a blind eye to a few flaws or difficulties...

636
00:51:58,280 --> 00:52:04,280
ちょっと甘え、甘えておりますのじゃ。
I'm just relying on your kindness here!

637
00:52:04,280 --> 00:52:11,480
甘えておりまして、まあだから、まあ難しいけど好きな曲を歌っちゃおうかな！
Relying on you, so... even though it's hard, I decided to sing a song I love!

638
00:52:11,580 --> 00:52:15,580
カラオケだし！と思って、歌わせていただきまーすのじゃ！
Thinking, "Hey, it's karaoke after all!" So allow me to sing it!

639
00:52:18,080 --> 00:52:22,080
ちなみに『SAKKAC CRAFT』の中でなんで「アノニマスファンファーレ」を持ってきたかと言うと。
By the way, speaking of why I picked "Anonymous Fanfare" out of SAKKAC CRAFT...

640
00:52:22,580 --> 00:52:30,080
なんか『SAKKAC CRAFT』を『SAKKAC CRAFT』たらしめる...なんじゃろうな？
It's like... what makes SAKKAC CRAFT truly SAKKAC CRAFT, you know?

641
00:52:30,280 --> 00:52:36,580
いや、全部好きなんだけどもちろんね。全部好きなんじゃが...
I mean, I love all of them of course! I love all the songs, but...

642
00:52:36,780 --> 00:52:43,580
『SAKKAC CRAFT』の顔だと思ってて、勝手に。
I personally feel like it's the signature face of SAKKAC CRAFT.

643
00:52:43,880 --> 00:52:50,080
なんか、あのツミキさんのボカロロックの...
It has all of Tsumiki-san's Vocalo-Rock essence...

644
00:52:50,180 --> 00:52:53,580
全て！全て！全てある！
Everything! Everything! It has everything!

645
00:52:53,880 --> 00:52:57,880
ガチで「アノニマスファンファーレ」って完全の曲だと思ってて。
Seriously, I consider "Anonymous Fanfare" to be a complete masterpiece.

646
00:52:58,080 --> 00:53:00,080
そう。
Yeah.

647
00:53:00,180 --> 00:53:03,280
一番完全ボカロロックだと思ってるから。
Because I think it's the ultimate embodiment of Vocalo-Rock.

648
00:53:04,080 --> 00:53:08,580
完全ボカロロックと思って選んできましたのじゃ。
That's why I chose it, believing it to be perfect Vocalo-Rock.

649
00:53:08,980 --> 00:53:12,880
オタク語りのじゃー！早口になると声のトーンがガチで変わる。
I'm full-on otaku chatting! When I talk fast, my tone of voice totally changes.

650
00:53:12,880 --> 00:53:17,580
やばい、オタクなのがバレちゃう。やめて！やめてほしいのじゃ！
Oh no, my otaku side is exposed. Stop it! Please don't look at me like that!

651
00:53:18,080 --> 00:53:22,280
可愛いって思われたいのにオタクなのバレちゃうのじゃー！
I wanted to be seen as cute, but my otaku side got exposed!

652
00:53:22,580 --> 00:53:24,080
それでは...
Well then...

653
00:53:24,880 --> 00:53:30,080
歌うのじゃー！頑張れわし！頑張れわし！
Time to sing! Do your best, me! Do your best, me!

654
00:53:30,180 --> 00:53:32,080
メラちゃん大好きありがとう！
"Love you Mela-chan", thank you!

655
00:53:30,680 --> 00:53:32,280
ワン、ツー、スリー、フォー！
One, two, three, four!

656
00:53:45,080 --> 00:53:51,580
（音量点検）マイクチェックワンツー聞こえるか、僕の存在証明讃歌が。
(Volume Check) Microphone test 1, 2, can you hear me? My hymn of proof of existence...

657
00:53:51,880 --> 00:53:57,680
師走の崩落はカラスの裡面二つが窺って死んだ。
The collapse in December, two crow internals peeked and died.

658
00:53:57,880 --> 00:54:01,880
ねぇねぇねぇ、僕は如何様？如何様？イカサマか？此れは電気朝霧のゲームだ。
Hey, hey, hey, what am I? What am I? A fraud? This is a game in the electric morning mist.

659
00:54:02,080 --> 00:54:06,580
欲張って頬張った、フラクタルは腐った様だった。
Greedy and stuffed full, the fractal seemed to have rotted.

660
00:54:06,880 --> 00:54:10,880
宙に舞って銃を持って、目が回ってしまうわブレイクダウン。
Dancing in the air, holding a gun, my head is spinning, breakdown.

661
00:54:10,980 --> 00:54:18,580
僕のせいと、騒いでいるのは誰？誰？寂しくなって、言葉を売って、呼吸と二人法制になって。
"It's my fault," who is raising a fuss? Who? Feeling lonely, selling words, making laws together with breath.

662
00:54:18,880 --> 00:54:26,980
最終回まで盲目、ずっと夢の中。声を枯らして、愛を謳って、結末を待っている。
Blind until the final episode, forever in a dream. Straining my voice, singing of love, waiting for the conclusion.

663
00:54:27,280 --> 00:54:34,080
さらば絶望的なハッピーエンド、クラップハンズなど必要無い無い無いわ！
Farewell to the desperate happy ending, there's no, no, no need for clapping hands!

664
00:54:51,880 --> 00:54:59,880
今に、ステップインツー！悲鳴鳴らす！僕は二十三、時計と愛。匿名の音楽は、肥育の飼い犬一つ孕んで飛んだ。
Now, step into! Sounding a scream! I am 23, clocks and love. Anonymous music soared carrying one fattened dog.

665
00:55:00,088 --> 00:55:01,988
んで飛んだ。歪んだ僕等なんだ。何様だ。
...and flew. We're distorted. Who do we think we are?

666
00:55:01,988 --> 00:55:05,188
これは半信半疑のルールだ。
These are rules of half-faith and half-doubt.

667
00:55:05,188 --> 00:55:09,188
散らかった弁は迷路のごとく、僕を惑わして、チャッチャッチャッ...
Scattered words confuse me like a maze, cha-cha-cha...

668
00:55:09,988 --> 00:55:14,388
点となって線となって、気が狂ってしまうわ ブレイクダウン。
Becoming dots, becoming lines, I'm going crazy, breakdown.

669
00:55:14,388 --> 00:55:18,288
全部全部間違っているのは、誰？誰？
Who's wrong about everything, everything? Who? Who?

670
00:55:18,288 --> 00:55:22,388
悲しくなって、言葉を売って、呼吸と二人ぼっちになって、
Becoming sad, selling words, left alone with just my breath...

671
00:55:22,388 --> 00:55:26,788
カーテンコールまで、秘密はきっと夜の中。
Until the curtain call, the secrets will surely stay in the night.

672
00:55:26,788 --> 00:55:30,388
目を瞑って、偽名を貼って、行場を探している。
Closing eyes, slapping on pseudonyms, searching for a place to go.

673
00:55:30,388 --> 00:55:36,988
さらば！絶望的なハッピーエンド。クラップハンズなど、必要ない！ない！ない！わ。
Farewell! Desperate happy ending. No need for clapping hands! No! No! No!

674
00:55:38,088 --> 00:55:40,888
ここ、ここガチで世界で一番いい。
This part right here is seriously the best in the world.

675
00:55:45,088 --> 00:55:46,388
マジでありがとう。
Thank you so much, seriously.

676
00:55:53,688 --> 00:55:57,988
名前を呼んで、僕を探して、帷で一人ぼっちになって、
Call my name, search for me, left alone in the curtain...

677
00:55:57,988 --> 00:56:02,888
エンドロールまで、記憶はずっと迷妄の中。
Until the end roll, memories remain lost in delusion.

678
00:56:02,888 --> 00:56:08,988
忘れないで、思い出して、鳴り響くファンファーレ！
Don't forget, remember, the fanfare echoing aloud!

679
00:56:08,988 --> 00:56:13,288
悲しくなって、言葉を売って、呼吸と二人ぼっちになって、
Becoming sad, selling words, left alone with just my breath...

680
00:56:13,288 --> 00:56:17,888
最終回まで、僕はずっと夢の中。
Until the final episode, I'm forever inside a dream.

681
00:56:17,888 --> 00:56:21,888
声を枯らして、愛を歌って、結末を待っている。
Straining my voice, singing of love, waiting for the ending.

682
00:56:21,888 --> 00:56:28,088
さらば！絶望的なハッピーエンド。クラップハンズなど、いらない！ない！ない！
Farewell! Desperate happy ending. No need for clapping hands! No! No! No!

683
00:56:28,088 --> 00:56:35,888
終生は其の素み付いた。病月と酷似している。三分と少しのエラーは、呼吸を開始した。
Life has taken root. Resembling a diseased moon. An error of three minutes and a bit began breathing.

684
00:56:36,588 --> 00:56:39,888
タッタタンタン、タッタッタタンタン。
Ta-ta-tan-tan, ta-ta-ta-tan-tan.

685
00:56:40,488 --> 00:56:41,588
えーっと...
Let's see...

686
00:56:43,988 --> 00:56:45,388
よいしょ。
Up we go.

687
00:56:45,488 --> 00:56:49,988
のじゃー！『アノニマスファンファレ』でしたのじゃー！
Noja~! That was 'Anonymous Fanfare', noja~!

688
00:56:51,188 --> 00:56:54,688
あのね、あの、おぬしら気づいとると思うんだけどね...
You know, I think you guys have noticed, but...

689
00:56:54,788 --> 00:56:58,288
わしの好きなボカロ曲ってね、高くて早いの。
The Vocaloid songs I like are high-pitched and fast.

690
00:56:59,888 --> 00:57:07,488
わしがね、わしが好きな曲ってね、高くて早いのじゃ。だから難しいの。
The songs I like are high-pitched and fast, noja. That's why they're so hard.

691
00:57:09,188 --> 00:57:15,388
「歌ってみた」とかね、綺麗にパッケージしてね、出したらいい感じなんじゃけど。
It'd be great if I could nicely package them for a cover video and release them, but...

692
00:57:16,888 --> 00:57:23,788
なかなか...なかなか難しい...難しいが、ガチで好きなの。ガチで好きなの。
They're pretty... pretty difficult. Difficult, but I seriously love them. I really do.

693
00:57:24,888 --> 00:57:29,088
「めらちの歌う曲で誕生日を迎えられて最高」本当！？じゃあ、おめでとうのアノニマスファンファレ！
"It's the best to welcome my birthday listening to Melachi's songs"? Really!? Then happy birthday with Anonymous Fanfare!

694
00:57:31,988 --> 00:57:35,088
お誕生日おめでとうなのじゃー！でも「クラップハンズなどいらない」って言ってるからな。
Happy birthday, noja~! Though the song says "No need for clapping hands".

695
00:57:35,388 --> 00:57:37,388
「いらない！ない！ない！」わーつってるからな。
Since it goes "No need! No! No!"

696
00:57:38,288 --> 00:57:40,788
おめでたいのじゃー！
Congrats, noja~!

697
00:57:43,088 --> 00:57:48,388
そう、ツミキさんの『SAKKAC CRAFT』ガチで全部...全部いい。
Yeah, Tsumiki's "SAKKAC CRAFT" album is seriously all... all good.

698
00:57:48,388 --> 00:57:53,388
全部良くて、全部大好き。わしの...あの、好きなアルバム一選。好きなアルバム一選なのじゃ。
Everything is great and I love all of it. It's one of my... absolute favorite albums, noja.

699
00:57:53,588 --> 00:57:55,288
ガチで好き。あの...
I seriously love it. Um...

700
00:57:56,188 --> 00:57:59,888
今日は、あの、『アノニマスファンファレ』入れたから...
Today, since I put 'Anonymous Fanfare' on the list...

701
00:58:00,188 --> 00:58:09,188
入れなかったけど、なんか『リローデッド』さんとかもめっちゃ好きじゃから、いつか歌枠で歌いたいなーって思うのじゃ。
I couldn't include it today, but I really like tracks like 'Reloaded' too, so I hope to sing them in a karaoke stream someday, noja.

702
00:58:12,688 --> 00:58:13,988
のじゃ。
Noja.

703
00:58:14,688 --> 00:58:16,488
そして、お次何歌うつもり...
And next, what was I planning to sing...

704
00:58:16,888 --> 00:58:21,088
あ！やばい！キャラソン来た！やばい、おぬしら！おぬしらさ！
Ah! Oh no! A character song is up! Oh no, guys! Hey, you guys!

705
00:58:22,088 --> 00:58:25,088
おぬしら本当にキャラソン歌い出していい？
Can I really start singing a character song?

706
00:58:25,288 --> 00:58:29,088
わしがキャラソン歌っても怒らない？
You won't get mad if I sing a character song?

707
00:58:30,088 --> 00:58:33,888
わしがキャラソン歌っても怒らない、おぬしら？
You won't get mad if I sing a character song, will you?

708
00:58:36,588 --> 00:58:38,988
きょー、今日は好きな曲歌っていい？
To-Today, can I sing my favorite songs?

709
00:58:41,388 --> 00:58:42,688
よし、それでは...
Alright, then...

710
00:58:45,088 --> 00:58:46,088
失礼して...
Excuse me...

711
00:58:48,088 --> 00:58:55,588
『残響・ダウルダブラ』を歌わせていただこうかなと、思いますのじゃ。
I think I shall sing 'Zankyou Daurdaebra', noja.

712
00:58:56,588 --> 00:58:57,688
失礼して...
Excuse me...

713
00:58:59,888 --> 00:59:02,588
キャラソン歌おうかなー。
I think I'll sing a character song~

714
00:59:03,988 --> 00:59:08,588
そう！シンフォギアの曲！キャラソン！
Yes! A Symphogear song! A character song!

715
00:59:09,988 --> 00:59:14,688
なのじゃ。歌わせていただきますのじゃー！
Noja. I shall sing it, noja~!

716
00:59:16,888 --> 00:59:19,488
よいしょ。BGMを切って...
Yoisho. Turning off the BGM...

717
00:59:19,788 --> 00:59:21,288
よいしょ。
Yoisho.

718
00:59:22,388 --> 00:59:25,088
歌うのじゃー！
I'm going to sing, noja~!

719
00:59:29,988 --> 00:59:31,488
かっこいいんじゃない？
Isn't it cool?

720
00:59:52,488 --> 00:59:57,388
嗚呼、終焉への輪舞曲が薫る。
Ah, the rondo leading to the end wafts by.

721
00:59:57,388 --> 01:00:00,096
殺戮の福音に...
In the gospel of slaughter...

722
01:00:00,096 --> 01:00:01,896
乞いん 契りへと散れ 血涙と散れ
Scatter into the vow... Scatter with tears of blood...

723
01:00:01,896 --> 01:00:06,896
微分子レベルまで解体して 反逆を永劫に断つ
Dissecting down to the subatomic level, severing rebellion for eternity...

724
01:00:06,896 --> 01:00:11,896
るLu RぃRぁ... 宇宙が傾き Rっる RぃRぁ... 太陽が凍る
Lu Ru Ri Ra... the universe tilts, Ru Ru Ri Ra... the sun freezes...

725
01:00:11,896 --> 01:00:18,596
Genocide & genocide

726
01:00:27,296 --> 01:00:32,496
血液一滴残さず 憎悪と力で掻き毟る
Without a single drop of blood remaining, clawing away with hatred and strength...

727
01:00:32,496 --> 01:00:37,396
震え悼め... 世界の崩れる Love song
Tremble and mourn... the love song of a collapsing world...

728
01:00:37,396 --> 01:00:44,296
奇跡など殺すと誓ったのだ
I swore to kill even miracles...

729
01:00:44,296 --> 01:00:54,096
想い出など微塵も焼き消して 狂い酔えば 来しの笑顔も
Burning away every shred of memories, intoxicating in madness, even past smiles...

730
01:00:54,096 --> 01:00:58,096
世界を壊す歌が 忘却へと
A song that destroys the world into oblivion...

731
01:00:58,096 --> 01:01:07,496
愛など見えない 愛などわからぬ 愛など終わらせる
I can't see love, I don't understand love, I will bring love to an end...

732
01:01:16,096 --> 01:01:25,096
鳴呼... 優しく触れていた 温かくぬくもったあの掌
Ah... the gentle touch, that palm filled with warmth...

733
01:01:25,096 --> 01:01:34,096
名前が... 思い出せやしない 枯れ果て尽くした心
I can't... remember the name, a heart completely withered away...

734
01:01:34,096 --> 01:01:40,096
るLu RぃRぁ... 業火のレクイエム るLu RぃRぁ... くるりと踊るの
Lu Ru Ri Ra... a requiem of hellfire, Lu Ru Ri Ra... dancing round and round...

735
01:01:40,096 --> 01:01:46,596
Genocide & genocide

736
01:01:49,896 --> 01:01:59,896
ドクンと脈打つすべてを 生きる万物すべてを 救済への階段から 突き落とせ...
Everything thrumming with a heartbeat, every living creature, cast them down from the stairs of salvation...

737
01:02:00,096 --> 01:02:09,696
虚無こそが安寧の楽園と 信じること以外に何があるか?
Is there anything to believe in other than void being the paradise of tranquility?

738
01:02:09,696 --> 01:02:19,496
万象の摂理を暴き歌う 0と1に掟した我が音楽
Uncovering the providence of all creation and singing, my music prescribed in 0s and 1s...

739
01:02:19,496 --> 01:02:30,496
愛など嗤う 愛した... 贖いを
Laughing at love... the atonement for having loved...

740
01:03:07,096 --> 01:03:11,096
るLu RぃRぁ... 消えてく... 抱かれてく... るLu RぃRぁ... 暮してく... 死んでく...
Lu Ru Ri Ra... vanishing... being embraced... Lu Ru Ri Ra... setting... dying...

741
01:03:11,096 --> 01:03:17,096
Genocide & genocide

742
01:03:21,096 --> 01:03:32,496
涙の一滴残さず絞った 怒号のカタストロフ 根底から完全否定して燃やせ
Wringing out without a single drop of tear left, the catastrophe of roaring fury, completely deny and burn it from the bottom...

743
01:03:33,096 --> 01:03:40,096
奇跡など殺すと誓ったのだ
I swore to kill even miracles...

744
01:03:40,096 --> 01:03:49,096
想い出など微塵も焼き消して 狂い酔えば 来しの笑顔も
Burning away every shred of memories, intoxicating in madness, even past smiles...

745
01:03:49,096 --> 01:03:54,096
世界を壊す歌が 忘却へと
A song that destroys the world into oblivion...

746
01:03:54,096 --> 01:04:05,096
愛していた日々 愛していた日々 故故... 永眠らせる
The days I loved, the days I loved, therefore... putting them to eternal sleep...

747
01:04:15,596 --> 01:04:22,096
のーじゃー！戦姫絶唱シンフォギアのキャロルじゃー！
Noja! That was Carol from Symphogear!

748
01:04:23,896 --> 01:04:33,596
コメントでバレてる。キャラソン歌うとき、あちちめらがキャラソン歌うとき、歌い方を寄せようと頑張っていることがバレているのじゃ。
I got exposed in the chat. They noticed that when Achichi Mela sings character songs, she tries her best to imitate the singing style.

749
01:04:34,596 --> 01:04:36,596
バレてる...
I got exposed...

750
01:04:39,096 --> 01:04:47,596
うん、すごいね。なんかね、シンフォギアね、キャラソンかっこいい系めちゃくちゃ多くてね、すごい好きなんだよね。
Yeah, it's impressive. You know, Symphogear has so many cool character songs, I really love them.

751
01:04:48,096 --> 01:05:00,096
そう、キャラソンというか... 劇中歌? なんか、ワシの認識なんじゃけど、あの... なんじゃろな...
Yeah, or rather than character songs... insert songs? At least in my understanding... what would it be...

752
01:05:00,104 --> 01:05:02,904
オープニング、エンディングがアニソンで、
The opening and ending themes are anime songs,

753
01:05:02,904 --> 01:05:10,104
それ以外のCV、キャラクターボイスの方が歌っていらっしゃるのが、
while songs sung by the voice actors for other roles...

754
01:05:11,904 --> 01:05:13,304
キャラソン。
...are character songs.

755
01:05:13,304 --> 01:05:15,904
何？「高くつくぜ、俺の歌は」？
What's that? "My song comes at a high price"?

756
01:05:20,704 --> 01:05:26,604
そうそうそう。テーマ的にもね、あの、なんじゃろな、
Right, right, right. In terms of themes too, well, how should I put it?

757
01:05:27,104 --> 01:05:28,504
高いんだよね。
The pitch is really high, right?

758
01:05:30,504 --> 01:05:33,304
そう。高いから...
Yeah, because it's so high...

759
01:05:36,104 --> 01:05:37,404
のいじゃ。
...noija.

760
01:05:40,104 --> 01:05:44,304
廣義的には声優さんが歌ったらキャラソン。
Broadly speaking, if a voice actor sings it, it's a character song.

761
01:05:48,104 --> 01:05:50,104
キャラソンめっちゃ好きなんだよね。
I really love character songs, you know?

762
01:05:50,104 --> 01:05:54,104
なんかね、わしね、あの、なんじゃろな...
For some reason, you see, how should I put it...

763
01:05:57,304 --> 01:06:02,604
もうサブスクとかにもリリースされてなくて、ブルーレイにしかついてこないキャラソンとかあるじゃん。
There are character songs that aren't even released on streaming services and only come with the Blu-rays, right?

764
01:06:02,904 --> 01:06:05,604
キャラソンがめちゃくちゃ好きでさ。
I just love character songs so much.

765
01:06:05,604 --> 01:06:08,604
そう、キャラソンを聴くのがめちゃくちゃ好きでさ。
Yeah, I love listening to character songs so much.

766
01:06:10,304 --> 01:06:14,304
だからその、いろんなアニメのキャラソンで好きなのめちゃくちゃいっぱいあるんじゃけど、
So, while I have tons of favorite character songs from various anime,

767
01:06:15,604 --> 01:06:21,104
大体ね、キャラソンはね、カラオケに入ってないことが多いんだよね。
character songs usually aren't available on karaoke systems most of the time.

768
01:06:21,604 --> 01:06:23,604
入ってないことが多いんだよな。
They're often not included, you know?

769
01:06:23,604 --> 01:06:29,104
だから歌いたくても歌えないみたいなことが結構あるんだよな。
So even if I want to sing them, I often can't.

770
01:06:30,104 --> 01:06:34,604
確かに、最近はもうキャラソンの文化があんまないか。悲しい話なのじゃ。
It's true that lately the character song culture isn't as prevalent anymore. That's so sad.

771
01:06:35,604 --> 01:06:40,604
え、そう！『ごちうさ』とか！そうそうそう！わしあれ好き。『魔女っ子ラビュっとちーの』好き。
Oh, right! Like "Gochiusa"! Yes, yes, yes! I love that one. I love "Majokko Rabyutto Chino".

772
01:06:41,104 --> 01:06:43,104
そうそうそう。
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

773
01:06:44,904 --> 01:06:50,604
え、そう、『シンフォギア』のさ、特典に入ってるのとかもある、あるよね。そうそうそうそう。
Oh right, like the ones included as bonus tracks in "Symphogear", right? Exactly, exactly.

774
01:06:54,104 --> 01:06:58,604
じゃからね、いっぱいね、今後ね、アニソンを歌いたい。
That's why I want to sing lots of anime songs in the future.

775
01:06:58,604 --> 01:07:04,604
ちょっとずつね。全曲キャラソンの歌枠とか大変じゃからね。
Bit by bit. Doing a karaoke stream with only character songs would be tough, after all.

776
01:07:04,604 --> 01:07:14,104
なんじゃろ、多くの中の一つ、多くの中の1つをね、こう入れていこうとね、思ってるのじゃ。
So I'm thinking of including one or two among the many songs I sing.

777
01:07:14,104 --> 01:07:19,604
そう！あの頃キャラソン作ってた人がね、今VTuberの楽曲作ってるんですよ。
Exactly! The people who made character songs back then are creating VTuber songs now.

778
01:07:20,104 --> 01:07:21,904
そう。嬉しい。
Yeah. I'm so happy.

779
01:07:22,604 --> 01:07:25,604
神が...ガチで、ガチで神が勝ってると思う。
Godly... I seriously, seriously think they're god-tier creators.

780
01:07:25,604 --> 01:07:28,104
神、神作家だらけで草。
It's hilarious how packed it is with god-tier composers.

781
01:07:28,104 --> 01:07:34,104
VTuberの、VTuber楽曲の提供作家ガチ神作家だらけでやばいのじゃ。
The composers providing VTuber songs are seriously all god-tier, it's amazing.

782
01:07:36,604 --> 01:07:37,904
大好きなのじゃ。
I love it so much.

783
01:07:38,304 --> 01:07:40,904
いつか作ってもらいたい...え、作ってもらいたいな。
I want them to make a song for me someday... Oh, I'd love that!

784
01:07:41,304 --> 01:07:45,104
わしも...いやわしガチでさ、もうこんなに...
Me too... honestly, since I've been watching/listening this much...

785
01:07:45,104 --> 01:07:53,104
見てれば、さすがにそろそろ皆様お気づきかと思いますが、あちちめらは実は曲が好きで...
...I'm sure everyone has realized by now, but Achichi Mela actually loves music...

786
01:07:54,104 --> 01:07:57,104
まだ気づいてない人はあんまいないかなとは思うんじゃが、
I don't think there's anyone who hasn't noticed yet, but...

787
01:07:57,104 --> 01:08:01,104
実はあちちめら、曲が好きで...
...in truth, Achichi Mela loves music...

788
01:08:03,104 --> 01:08:07,104
実はね、実は。そう。
Actually, you know? Actually. Yeah.

789
01:08:07,104 --> 01:08:14,104
かなり実は曲が好きだし、ボカロPさんも好きだし、作家さんも好きだし、
I really love songs, I love Vocaloid producers, and I love composers,

790
01:08:14,104 --> 01:08:15,604
で...
and...

791
01:08:16,104 --> 01:08:20,604
だから、あちちめらももちろんオリ曲いっぱい作りたい。
so of course Achichi Mela wants to make lots of original songs too!

792
01:08:21,104 --> 01:08:24,104
うん、オリ曲をいっぱい作りたい。
Yeah, I want to make lots of original songs.

793
01:08:24,104 --> 01:08:26,604
ライブとかもしたいけど、
I want to hold live concerts and stuff too, but...

794
01:08:27,104 --> 01:08:34,104
正直ライブしたい...もちろんその先にライブがあるのはすごい嬉しいんじゃが、曲をね、発注したい！
honestly, doing live shows... while having lives ahead is great, I really want to commission songs!

795
01:08:34,104 --> 01:08:42,104
好きな作家さんに自分の思った、好きの、わしの考える最強の楽曲を作ってもらいたい。
I want my favorite composers to write the ultimate song that I envision and love!

796
01:08:42,604 --> 01:08:48,904
そう。あるの。「こういう曲作りたいな」みたいなのがめちゃくちゃあって。
Yeah. I have so many ideas like, "I want to make a song like this!"

797
01:08:48,904 --> 01:08:52,104
めちゃくちゃ...やっぱね、いや、おぬしらもさ...
So many... after all, you guys do it too, right...?

798
01:08:52,104 --> 01:09:00,104
オタク君としてこうさ、音楽を聴いてる中でさ、「わ、この曲いいな。わしだったらこの曲はライブのセトリのこの辺に持っていくな」とか思いながら聴くじゃろ？
As music otaku listening to music, you listen thinking, "Wow, this song is great. If it were me, I'd put this near this part of a live setlist," right?

799
01:09:00,104 --> 01:09:06,104
おぬしら、おぬしらさ、好きな曲とかをさ、自分、別にライブしないのにセットリスト作ったりするじゃろ？好きな曲で。
You guys, even though you don't perform live yourselves, make setlists with your favorite songs, right?

800
01:09:06,104 --> 01:09:13,104
「あ、ちょっとこれはライブのこの辺に入れたら熱いですね」とか、「ダブルアンコールにこれ欲しいですね」とか考えるじゃろ？やるでしょ？やるじゃろ？
You think, "Ah, it'd be hype to put this here in a live," or "I want this for a double encore," right? You do that, don't you?

801
01:09:14,104 --> 01:09:19,604
ミットとか、うわーな...みたいな感じで、わしは曲を聴きながら「うわ、このボカロPさんは...」
Like middle songs, or "Whoa..." and so while listening to music, I think, "Wow, this Vocaloid producer..."

802
01:09:19,604 --> 01:09:28,104
ボカロPさんとか結構テイストが分かりやすいから、「うわ、この人こういう系が得意だから、わしだったらこの人のこういう系が見たいな」みたいに...
Vocaloid producers often have very recognizable styles, so I think, "Wow, since they're good at this style, I'd love to see them do this kind of track for me."

803
01:09:28,104 --> 01:09:37,104
そう、まあ、だから、わしへの提供じゃなくて、もう、その企画をそのまま渡してそれをそのまま作って自分の曲として出していただいても構わない...
So, even if it's not provided to me, I wouldn't mind handing over the concept for them to produce and release as their own song...

804
01:09:37,104 --> 01:09:42,104
もちろん構わない、それですごい嬉しいのシステム...違う違う、早く早く、のじゃのじゃのじゃのじゃ...のじゃー！
Of course I'd be happy with that! Wait, no no, hurry up... noja noja noja... noja!

805
01:09:42,104 --> 01:09:46,104
いや、何が言いたいかと言うと、
I mean, what I want to say is,

806
01:09:46,104 --> 01:09:52,104
あの、曲を聴きながら「うわ、この人はこういう曲が得意だからわしこういうの頼みたいな」みたいなのがいっぱいあるの！
while listening to music, I have so many ideas like, "Oh, this person excels at this, so I'd love to request something like that!"

807
01:09:52,104 --> 01:09:59,904
「この人にはこれ頼みたい、この人にはこれ頼みたい、この人はこういうのが得意だからこうしたら多分もっといいのができる」みたいなさ、そういうのがめちゃくちゃ思いつくのじゃ！
"I want to request this from this person, and that from that person; they're great at this, so if we do it like that, it'll turn out even better!" I come up with so many ideas like that!

808
01:10:00,224 --> 01:10:01,412
そう。
Yeah.

809
01:10:02,912 --> 01:10:04,212
だから...
So...

810
01:10:04,712 --> 01:10:09,712
まあまあまあ、だから... やっぱ、こうね... いずれね、一般公募曲とかもね、出したいなって思ってるの。
Well, anyway, so... after all, I'm thinking I'd like to release songs through public commissions someday.

811
01:10:10,612 --> 01:10:12,812
頼みたいものが... いっぱいなのじゃ！
There are so many things I want to ask for!

812
01:10:13,212 --> 01:10:15,612
え、だって夢じゃない？ 夢じゃない？ おぬしら考えてみ。
I mean, isn't that a dream? Isn't it? Just think about it, everyone.

813
01:10:15,912 --> 01:10:22,312
自分の好きなさ... 自分の好きな作家さんにさ、自分がさ、好きなようにさ発注できるんだよ？
You get to commission your favorite... your favorite creators to make whatever you like, you know?

814
01:10:22,412 --> 01:10:28,312
「こういう曲が作りたくて」「こういう歌詞を入れたくて」「こういうことをしたくて」みたいな、「こういう、あの、編曲でお願いしたくて」みたいな...
Like, "I want to make this kind of song," "I want these lyrics," "I want to do this," "I'd like this kind of arrangement," and so on...

815
01:10:28,412 --> 01:10:32,512
そういうのをさ、言えるのガチ... ガチで神で笑った。なんかもう、「い-いいんですか？」
Being able to say all that is seriously... seriously god-tier, it made me laugh. It's like, "I-Is this really okay?"

816
01:10:32,612 --> 01:10:37,912
「オタク君の... ぼ-僕の考える最強のまるまるを、あの、再現していただいていいのですか？」って思うんだけど...
"Can you really reproduce the ultimate... the ultimate ideal song that this otaku came up with?" is what I feel, but...

817
01:10:38,312 --> 01:10:45,612
ちょっと... ちょっとそれって... それでちょっと... なんか... 職権乱用オタク君すぎます、私利私欲オタク君すぎませんか？と思いつつ...
Isn't that... isn't that a bit... like, abusing my position as an otaku, being way too selfish for an otaku? While thinking that...

818
01:10:45,712 --> 01:10:47,912
思いつつ！ わしそれなの！ わしそれなのじゃ！
While thinking that, that's totally me! That's totally who I am!

819
01:10:48,112 --> 01:10:51,212
そう！ だから... ガチで楽しみ！
Exactly! So... I'm seriously looking forward to it!

820
01:10:52,112 --> 01:10:55,812
ガチでオリ曲出すの... ガチで楽しみなのじゃ。
Releasing an original song is... something I'm seriously looking forward to.

821
01:10:56,312 --> 01:10:58,312
夢ある。超夢ある。
It's full of dreams. So full of dreams.

822
01:10:59,312 --> 01:11:00,712
もう... 嬉しい。
I'm just... so happy.

823
01:11:01,012 --> 01:11:04,212
もう... こ-これ以上の喜び... ない、世界に。実は。
Honestly, there's no... no greater joy than this in the world, actually.

824
01:11:04,312 --> 01:11:07,912
実は... 実はこれ以上の喜びって世界になくて。
Actually... actually, there's no greater joy in this world.

825
01:11:09,112 --> 01:11:12,112
そ... そう... すごい... すごい楽しみなのじゃ。
Y-Yeah... I'm really... really looking forward to it.

826
01:11:15,212 --> 01:11:17,912
にゃー、そうそうそう。ホロ... ホロどりです。
Meow, yeah yeah yeah. Holo... Holodori.

827
01:11:18,112 --> 01:11:20,412
ホロ... もちろんホロどりにも入りたいのじゃ。
Holo... Of course I want to join Holodori too.

828
01:11:20,612 --> 01:11:23,112
もちろんホロどりとしても楽曲出させていただきたいです。
Of course, I'd also like to release songs as part of Holodori.

829
01:11:23,312 --> 01:11:26,612
実装も... あの、くいっくいっくいっ、お待ちしておりますのじゃ。
I'm eagerly awaiting its implementation, nudge nudge.

830
01:11:28,212 --> 01:11:31,812
そして、あと1曲用意してきたの、おぬしら！
And I've prepared one more song, everyone!

831
01:11:33,312 --> 01:11:36,612
あと1曲用意してきたの。まだまだ歌ってもいいが...
I prepared one more song. I could keep singing more, but...

832
01:11:36,812 --> 01:11:40,912
なんかね、今日22時からの配信あったんだけどね、なくなったからね、まだまだ歌ってもいいの記述が...
You see, I had a stream scheduled for 22:00 today, but it got canceled, so I could keep singing...

833
01:11:41,112 --> 01:11:43,812
とりあえず、あと1曲だけPNG用意してきた。
But anyway, I've prepared a PNG for just one more song.

834
01:11:44,112 --> 01:11:48,112
10日PNGに... 10日PNGを用意してきた...
Prepared a 10th anniversary PNG... a transparent PNG...

835
01:11:50,112 --> 01:11:55,112
1曲があり... そう、あるので...
There's one song... so, since I have it...

836
01:11:57,112 --> 01:11:59,912
ど-どうじゃ？ 予想とかする？
H-How about it? Want to make guesses?

837
01:12:00,112 --> 01:12:03,312
おぬしら... おぬしら予想とかしてみる？
Everyone... do you want to try guessing?

838
01:12:07,912 --> 01:12:09,612
喉... 喉はまだ大丈夫。
My throat... my throat is still fine.

839
01:12:09,912 --> 01:12:12,912
今のところ大丈夫だけど。
It's fine for now.

840
01:12:14,112 --> 01:12:16,912
えっと、あ、秋ねた始動... えっと...
Um, ah, people are getting bored... Um...

841
01:12:17,112 --> 01:12:18,612
アニソンです！
It's an anime song!

842
01:12:18,912 --> 01:12:22,612
アニソンであり... キャラソンです！
It's an anime song... and a character song!

843
01:12:23,112 --> 01:12:24,912
キャラソンです！
It's a character song!

844
01:12:25,112 --> 01:12:28,612
ボカロではありません！ ボカロではありません！
It's not Vocaloid! It's not Vocaloid!

845
01:12:29,112 --> 01:12:31,112
え、そして、デュエット曲です！
And, um, it's a duet song!

846
01:12:32,912 --> 01:12:35,912
デュエット曲... で...
A duet song... and...

847
01:12:36,712 --> 01:12:40,612
高くて早い... 高... 高いか？ 高くはないと思う。
High and fast... High... Is it high? I don't think it's high.

848
01:12:40,912 --> 01:12:44,912
先ほど... のものよりは... 高くないけど、あの、早いです！
Compared to... the previous ones... it's not high, but it's fast!

849
01:12:45,112 --> 01:12:47,912
早いですのじゃ！
It's fast!

850
01:12:50,112 --> 01:12:52,912
で、デュエットのキャラソンで...
And, as a duet character song...

851
01:12:53,112 --> 01:12:59,612
結構なんかセリフっぽい感じ... セリフっぽい感じ... です。
It's kind of... spoken-line-like... has spoken-like lines... in it.

852
01:13:07,112 --> 01:13:09,612
早くてデュエット。
Fast and a duet.

853
01:13:09,912 --> 01:13:13,912
っ！ 答え... 答え出た！ 答え出た！ 答え出たよ、おぬしら！
Ah! The answer... someone got it! Someone got it! Someone got the answer, everyone!

854
01:13:14,112 --> 01:13:18,912
答え出たよ！ 当ててる人いた！ きたー！ くふっ、当ててる人いた！
Someone got it! There was someone who guessed right! Here it is! Hehe, someone got it right!

855
01:13:19,112 --> 01:13:20,112
はい。
Yes.

856
01:13:20,312 --> 01:13:24,112
そして... えー... 大ヒント何かな？ 大ヒントは...
And... um... what would be a big hint? A big hint is...

857
01:13:24,612 --> 01:13:30,912
まあ、作曲者さんがまあ、ボカロP... ボカロPと言えばボカロPか？
Well, the composer is a Vocaloid producer... Well, can you call them a Vocaloid producer?

858
01:13:31,112 --> 01:13:36,612
まあ、ボカロPでもあるか。ボカロも出してる方が作曲者。
Well, they are also a Vocaloid producer. Someone who also releases Vocaloid songs is the composer.

859
01:13:37,112 --> 01:13:38,312
はい。
Yes.

860
01:13:39,112 --> 01:13:40,412
お、一人で歌います。
Oh, I'll sing it solo.

861
01:13:40,612 --> 01:13:44,312
次の曲はこちら！ デデデデデデ...
Here is the next song! Ta-da-da-da-da-da...

862
01:13:44,612 --> 01:13:52,612
はい！ 当ててる人いましたー！ 当ててる人がいましたよー！ 『スーパーウルトラハイパーミラクルロマンチック』を歌うのじゃー！
Yes! Someone guessed it right! Someone actually got it right! I'm going to sing "Super Ultra Hyper Miracle Romantic"!

863
01:13:53,112 --> 01:13:59,112
ん、答え出たよ。や、やるやん。やるやおぬしって思った。
Yeah, the answer came out. Wow, impressive. I was like, "You're good, impressive!"

864
01:14:00,112 --> 01:14:03,912
ちょっとタイトル長いんだけど。タイトル長いから2行にしちゃった。
The title is a bit long though. It's so long that I made it two lines.

865
01:14:04,112 --> 01:14:07,912
あの、カラスヤサボウさんの曲なのじゃ。
Um, it's a song by Karasuya Sabou.

866
01:14:09,112 --> 01:14:10,112
歌うか。
Shall I sing it?

867
01:14:11,112 --> 01:14:21,112
ちょっと、正直... 正直今のヒントだったら、あの、当てはまるものが多すぎて、むずいと思う。当てるのむずいと思う。
Honestly... honestly, with the hints I gave, there were way too many possibilities, so I thought it'd be tough. Tough to guess.

868
01:14:22,112 --> 01:14:24,112
そう、当ててる人すごい。
Yeah, the person who guessed it is amazing.

869
01:14:24,312 --> 01:14:27,912
タイガのね... 行くなじゃー！ よいしょー！
Taiga's... Here we go! Yoisho!

870
01:14:28,112 --> 01:14:30,112
いけるかな？
Can I do this?

871
01:14:31,612 --> 01:14:33,612
[Title: スーパーウルトラハイパーミラクルロマンチック]
[Title: Super Ultra Hyper Miracle Romantic]

872
01:14:34,112 --> 01:14:35,612
いきます！
Here I go!

873
01:14:44,312 --> 01:14:48,912
スーパーウルトラハイパーミラクルロマンチック！
Super Ultra Hyper Miracle Romantic!

874
01:14:49,912 --> 01:14:55,412
ズキュン ズキュン ズキュキュキュン ズキュン ズキュン ズキュキュキュン ズキュン！
Zukyun zukyun zukyukyukyun zukyun zukyun zukyukyukyun zukyun!

875
01:14:56,112 --> 01:15:00,112
ドキドキがバキバキで このままどうにかなっちゃいそう
My heart is pounding so hard, I feel like I'm gonna go crazy

876
